  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001080328', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000010803', 'very_hard', 1, 'Look at the bag. You take one counter. Which are true? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"Taking red might happen"},{"id":"b","text":"Taking blue might happen"},{"id":"c","text":"Taking green won''t happen"},{"id":"d","text":"Taking red will happen"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'There are red and blue counters, so each might happen. There is no green, so green won''t happen. Red is not sure, because you might get blue.', '{"kind":"bag","counters":[{"colour":"red","count":3},{"colour":"blue","count":3}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001080329', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000010803', 'very_hard', 1, 'Jai says, ''It will rain at lunchtime tomorrow.'' Which word should he use instead of ''will''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"might"},{"id":"b","text":"won''t"},{"id":"c","text":"always"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Nobody knows for sure if it will rain, so ''might'' is the right word.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001080330', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000010803', 'very_hard', 1, 'Look at the spinner. Mrs Lee wants landing on yellow to be something that won''t happen. What should she do?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Change the yellow part to green"},{"id":"b","text":"Add another yellow part"},{"id":"c","text":"Do nothing"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'If there is no yellow at all, landing on yellow won''t happen.', '{"kind":"spinner","sections":["green","green","green","yellow"]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_easy', 1, 'What sound does ''cat'' start with?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"c"},{"id":"b","text":"t"},{"id":"c","text":"a"},{"id":"d","text":"d"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Say it slowly: c-a-t. The first sound is c.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_easy', 1, '''Sun'' and ''sock'' start with the same sound.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Say them: s-un, s-ock. Both start with the s sound.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_easy', 1, 'c + a + t = ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"cat"'::jsonb, 'Say each sound, then push them together: c-a-t, cat.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'easy', 1, 'Which word rhymes with ''hat''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"hot"},{"id":"b","text":"mat"},{"id":"c","text":"hit"},{"id":"d","text":"ham"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Rhyming words end the same way. Hat and mat both end in -at.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'easy', 1, 'What is the last sound in ''dog''? Write the letter.', 'short_answer', NULL, '"g"'::jsonb, 'Say it slowly: d-o-g. The last sound is g.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'easy', 1, 'Which words start with ''sh''? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"ship"},{"id":"b","text":"shop"},{"id":"c","text":"chip"},{"id":"d","text":"sun"},{"id":"e","text":"shell"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","e"]'::jsonb, 'Ship, shop and shell start with sh. Chip starts with ch and sun starts with s.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'medium', 1, 'Which word has the ''ee'' sound, like in ''tree''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"bed"},{"id":"b","text":"feet"},{"id":"c","text":"fit"},{"id":"d","text":"fat"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Feet has ee in the middle: f-ee-t. It sounds like the ee in tree.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'medium', 1, 'ch + i + p = ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"chip"'::jsonb, 'The two letters ch make one sound. Blend it: ch-i-p, chip.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'medium', 1, 'Put the sounds in order to make ''fish''.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"f"},{"id":"b","text":"i"},{"id":"c","text":"sh"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'Say it slowly: f-i-sh. The sh makes one sound at the end.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'hard', 1, 'How many syllables (claps) are in ''rabbit''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"1"},{"id":"b","text":"2"},{"id":"c","text":"3"},{"id":"d","text":"4"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Clap it as you say it: rab-bit. That is two claps, so two syllables.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'hard', 1, 'Which words rhyme with ''cake''? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"lake"},{"id":"b","text":"make"},{"id":"c","text":"cook"},{"id":"d","text":"bake"},{"id":"e","text":"back"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Lake, make and bake all end in -ake, like cake. Cook and back end differently.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'hard', 1, 'The word ''duck'' ends with the letters ''ck''.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Duck is spelt d-u-c-k. The c and k together make one sound.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which word has three syllables?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"dog"},{"id":"b","text":"kitten"},{"id":"c","text":"kangaroo"},{"id":"d","text":"apple"}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, 'Clap each word. Kan-ga-roo has three claps. Kit-ten and ap-ple have two. Dog has one.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_hard', 1, 'Change the ''sh'' in ''shop'' to ''ch''. What word do you make?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"chop"'::jsonb, 'Take away sh and put ch at the start: ch-o-p, chop.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which words have the same middle sound as ''rain''? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"train"},{"id":"b","text":"pain"},{"id":"c","text":"ran"},{"id":"d","text":"snail"},{"id":"e","text":"rat"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Train, pain and snail have the ai sound, like rain. Ran and rat have a short a sound.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which letter does ''pig'' start with?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"b"},{"id":"b","text":"p"},{"id":"c","text":"g"},{"id":"d","text":"d"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Say it slowly: p-i-g. The first sound is p.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_easy', 1, 'm + o + p = ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"mop"'::jsonb, 'Say each sound, then push them together: m-o-p, mop.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_easy', 1, '''Bat'' and ''cat'' rhyme.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Bat and cat both end in -at, so they rhyme.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'easy', 1, 'Which word starts with ''th''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"thin"},{"id":"b","text":"tin"},{"id":"c","text":"fin"},{"id":"d","text":"chin"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Thin starts with th. Tin starts with t, fin with f and chin with ch.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'easy', 1, 'What is the first sound in ''moon''? Write the letter.', 'short_answer', NULL, '"m"'::jsonb, 'Say it slowly: m-oo-n. The first sound is m.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'easy', 1, 'Which words rhyme with ''pig''? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"dig"},{"id":"b","text":"big"},{"id":"c","text":"peg"},{"id":"d","text":"wig"},{"id":"e","text":"pin"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Dig, big and wig all end in -ig, like pig. Peg and pin end differently.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'medium', 1, 'Which word has the ''oo'' sound, like in ''moon''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"spoon"},{"id":"b","text":"sun"},{"id":"c","text":"pan"},{"id":"d","text":"pen"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Spoon has oo in the middle: sp-oo-n. It sounds like the oo in moon.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'medium', 1, 'Put the sounds in order to make ''chick''.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"ch"},{"id":"b","text":"i"},{"id":"c","text":"ck"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'Say it slowly: ch-i-ck. Ch makes the first sound and ck makes the last sound.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'medium', 1, '''Ship'' starts with the ''ch'' sound.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'Ship starts with sh: sh-i-p. Chip starts with ch.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'hard', 1, 'How many syllables (claps) are in ''butterfly''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"1"},{"id":"b","text":"2"},{"id":"c","text":"3"},{"id":"d","text":"4"}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, 'Clap it as you say it: but-ter-fly. That is three claps.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'hard', 1, 'Fill in the missing sound. A farm animal that says baa is a sh___p.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"ee"'::jsonb, 'The animal is a sheep: sh-ee-p. The missing sound is ee.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'hard', 1, 'Which words have ''th'' in them? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"bath"},{"id":"b","text":"bat"},{"id":"c","text":"three"},{"id":"d","text":"tree"},{"id":"e","text":"moth"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c","e"]'::jsonb, 'Bath, three and moth all have th. Bat and tree only have a t.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_hard', 1, 'Take the ''p'' off ''pink''. What word is left?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"ink"'::jsonb, 'Pink is p-ink. Take away the p and you have ink.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which word has a different middle sound from the others?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"feet"},{"id":"b","text":"seen"},{"id":"c","text":"bed"},{"id":"d","text":"green"}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, 'Feet, seen and green all have the ee sound. Bed has a short e sound, so it is different.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011101', 'very_hard', 1, 'Put these words in order from fewest to most syllables.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"cat"},{"id":"b","text":"tiger"},{"id":"c","text":"kangaroo"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'Clap each word. Cat has one clap, ti-ger has two and kan-ga-roo has three.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110201', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which word is spelt right?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"teh"},{"id":"b","text":"the"},{"id":"c","text":"hte"},{"id":"d","text":"eth"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, '''The'' is spelt t-h-e. It is a word we use all the time.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110202', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_easy', 1, 'One dog, two ___.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '["dogs"]'::jsonb, 'Add -s to show more than one: one dog, two dogs.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110203', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_easy', 1, '''Cat'' is spelt c-a-t.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Say it slowly: c-a-t. Each sound has one letter.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110204', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'easy', 1, 'Which is the right way to spell ''said''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"sed"},{"id":"b","text":"said"},{"id":"c","text":"sayd"},{"id":"d","text":"siad"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, '''Said'' is a tricky word. It is spelt s-a-i-d.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110205', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'easy', 1, 'Add -ing to ''jump''.', 'short_answer', NULL, '"jumping"'::jsonb, 'Just add -ing to the end: jump + ing = jumping.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110206', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'easy', 1, 'Which words are spelt right? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"was"},{"id":"b","text":"wos"},{"id":"c","text":"you"},{"id":"d","text":"yoo"},{"id":"e","text":"are"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c","e"]'::jsonb, 'Was, you and are are tricky words. Learn them by heart: w-a-s, y-o-u, a-r-e.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110207', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'medium', 1, 'play + ed = ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"played"'::jsonb, 'Just add -ed to the end: play + ed = played.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110208', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'medium', 1, 'Which word fits? ''I can see two ___.''', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"bird"},{"id":"b","text":"birds"},{"id":"c","text":"birdz"},{"id":"d","text":"brids"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'There are two, so we need more than one. Add -s: birds.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110209', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'medium', 1, 'Put the letters in order to spell ''ship''.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"s"},{"id":"b","text":"h"},{"id":"c","text":"i"},{"id":"d","text":"p"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'Say it slowly: sh-i-p. Sh is spelt with s then h.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110210', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'hard', 1, 'Add -ed to ''kick''.', 'short_answer', NULL, '"kicked"'::jsonb, 'Just add -ed to the end: kick + ed = kicked.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110211', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'hard', 1, 'The word ''have'' ends with the letter ''e''.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, '''Have'' is spelt h-a-v-e. You cannot hear the e, but it is there.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110212', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'hard', 1, 'Which word fits? ''Yesterday I ___ to my friend.''', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"talk"},{"id":"b","text":"talked"},{"id":"c","text":"talking"},{"id":"d","text":"talks"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Yesterday is in the past, so add -ed: talked.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110213', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which words are spelt right? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"going"},{"id":"b","text":"goeing"},{"id":"c","text":"jumped"},{"id":"d","text":"jumpt"},{"id":"e","text":"looking"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c","e"]'::jsonb, 'Going, jumped and looking just add -ing or -ed to the word. Goeing and jumpt are not right.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110214', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_hard', 1, 'Tom is ___ a book. (read + ing)', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"reading"'::jsonb, 'Just add -ing to read: reading. Tom is reading a book.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110215', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which word is spelt right?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"frend"},{"id":"b","text":"friend"},{"id":"c","text":"freind"},{"id":"d","text":"frind"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, '''Friend'' is a tricky word: f-r-i-e-n-d. Remember ''i before e'' in friend.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110216', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which word is spelt right?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"dog"},{"id":"b","text":"dgo"},{"id":"c","text":"odg"},{"id":"d","text":"gdo"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Say it slowly: d-o-g. The letters go in that order.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110217', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_easy', 1, 'One hat, two ___.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '["hats"]'::jsonb, 'Add -s to show more than one: one hat, two hats.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110218', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_easy', 1, '''Is'' is spelt i-z.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, '''Is'' sounds like it ends in z, but it is spelt i-s.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110219', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'easy', 1, 'look + ing = ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"looking"'::jsonb, 'Just add -ing to the end: look + ing = looking.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110220', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'easy', 1, 'Which is the right way to spell ''when''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"wen"},{"id":"b","text":"whenn"},{"id":"c","text":"when"},{"id":"d","text":"wehn"}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, '''When'' starts with wh: w-h-e-n.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110221', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'easy', 1, 'More than one ''cup'' is ''cups''.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Add -s to show more than one: one cup, two cups.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110222', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'medium', 1, 'Add -ed to ''help''.', 'short_answer', NULL, '"helped"'::jsonb, 'Just add -ed to the end: help + ed = helped.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110223', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'medium', 1, 'Which words mean more than one? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"cats"},{"id":"b","text":"bed"},{"id":"c","text":"pens"},{"id":"d","text":"frogs"},{"id":"e","text":"sun"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'Cats, pens and frogs end in -s, so they mean more than one. Bed and sun mean just one.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110224', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'medium', 1, 'Put the letters in order to spell ''much''.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"m"},{"id":"b","text":"u"},{"id":"c","text":"c"},{"id":"d","text":"h"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'Say it slowly: m-u-ch. Ch is spelt with c then h.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110225', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'hard', 1, 'Which is the right way to spell ''come''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"cum"},{"id":"b","text":"come"},{"id":"c","text":"kom"},{"id":"d","text":"coom"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, '''Come'' is a tricky word: c-o-m-e. It ends with an e.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110226', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'hard', 1, 'Yesterday we ___ to the shop. (walk + ed)', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"walked"'::jsonb, 'It happened yesterday, so add -ed: walk + ed = walked.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110227', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'hard', 1, 'Write the word for more than one ''book''.', 'short_answer', NULL, '"books"'::jsonb, 'Add -s to show more than one: one book, two books.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110228', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which words are spelt right? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"they"},{"id":"b","text":"thay"},{"id":"c","text":"here"},{"id":"d","text":"heer"},{"id":"e","text":"some"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c","e"]'::jsonb, 'They, here and some are tricky words: t-h-e-y, h-e-r-e, s-o-m-e.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110229', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which sentence is spelt right?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"I am runing."},{"id":"b","text":"I am running."},{"id":"c","text":"I am rnning."},{"id":"d","text":"I am runeing."}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Run has a short u, so we double the n before -ing: running.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001110230', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011102', 'very_hard', 1, 'The dogs are ___ in the park. (bark + ing)', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"barking"'::jsonb, 'Just add -ing to bark: barking. The dogs are barking.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_easy', 1, 'What is the opposite of ''big''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"large"},{"id":"b","text":"small"},{"id":"c","text":"tall"},{"id":"d","text":"fat"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Big and small are opposites. Large means the same as big.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_easy', 1, 'A puppy is a baby dog.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A baby dog is called a puppy.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_easy', 1, 'In ''the red ball'', which word is a describing word?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the"},{"id":"b","text":"red"},{"id":"c","text":"ball"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Red tells us what the ball looks like. It is a describing word.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'easy', 1, 'The opposite of ''up'' is ___.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"down"'::jsonb, 'If you are not going up, you are going down.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'easy', 1, 'Which of these are fruits? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"apple"},{"id":"b","text":"banana"},{"id":"c","text":"chair"},{"id":"d","text":"pear"},{"id":"e","text":"car"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Apples, bananas and pears are fruits you can eat. A chair and a car are not.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'easy', 1, 'Which word goes with ''knife and ___''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"fork"},{"id":"b","text":"shoe"},{"id":"c","text":"tree"},{"id":"d","text":"bus"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'We eat with a knife and fork. They go together.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'medium', 1, 'What does ''tiny'' mean?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"very small"},{"id":"b","text":"very big"},{"id":"c","text":"very fast"},{"id":"d","text":"very loud"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Tiny means very, very small, like an ant.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'medium', 1, 'What is the opposite of ''happy''?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["sad","unhappy","upset"]'::jsonb, 'When you are not happy, you are sad. Happy and sad are opposites.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'medium', 1, 'Put these animals in order from smallest to biggest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"ant"},{"id":"b","text":"cat"},{"id":"c","text":"horse"},{"id":"d","text":"elephant"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'An ant is tiny. A cat is bigger. A horse is bigger again. An elephant is the biggest.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'hard', 1, 'Which words tell how something feels when you touch it? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"soft"},{"id":"b","text":"rough"},{"id":"c","text":"red"},{"id":"d","text":"smooth"},{"id":"e","text":"loud"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Soft, rough and smooth tell how things feel. Red is a colour and loud is a sound.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'hard', 1, '''The koala was sleepy.'' What does ''sleepy'' mean?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"tired"},{"id":"b","text":"hungry"},{"id":"c","text":"angry"},{"id":"d","text":"wet"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Sleepy means you are tired and want to sleep.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'hard', 1, '''Shout'' and ''whisper'' mean the same thing.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'Shout means speak very loudly. Whisper means speak very quietly. They are opposites.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which word does NOT belong?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"red"},{"id":"b","text":"blue"},{"id":"c","text":"green"},{"id":"d","text":"round"}]'::jsonb, '"d"'::jsonb, 'Red, blue and green are colours. Round is a shape word, so it does not belong.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_hard', 1, '''Mum said the soup was boiling.'' What does ''boiling'' tell you?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"it was very hot"},{"id":"b","text":"it was very cold"},{"id":"c","text":"it was very old"},{"id":"d","text":"it was very sweet"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Boiling is when water bubbles because it is so hot. The soup was very hot.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_hard', 1, 'Put these in order from slowest to fastest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"snail"},{"id":"b","text":"rabbit"},{"id":"c","text":"racing car"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'A snail is very slow. A rabbit can hop fast. A racing car is the fastest.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_easy', 1, 'What is the opposite of ''hot''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"cold"},{"id":"b","text":"warm"},{"id":"c","text":"sunny"},{"id":"d","text":"wet"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Hot and cold are opposites.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_easy', 1, 'A joey is a baby kangaroo.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A baby kangaroo is called a joey. It lives in its mother''s pouch.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_easy', 1, 'The opposite of ''yes'' is ___.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"no"'::jsonb, 'Yes and no are opposites.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'easy', 1, 'Which word goes with ''salt and ___''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"pepper"},{"id":"b","text":"sugar"},{"id":"c","text":"sand"},{"id":"d","text":"milk"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'We often put salt and pepper on food. They go together.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'easy', 1, 'Which of these are animals? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"wombat"},{"id":"b","text":"kite"},{"id":"c","text":"emu"},{"id":"d","text":"table"},{"id":"e","text":"possum"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c","e"]'::jsonb, 'Wombats, emus and possums are Australian animals. A kite and a table are things.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'easy', 1, 'Which word means the same as ''glad''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"happy"},{"id":"b","text":"sad"},{"id":"c","text":"tired"},{"id":"d","text":"cross"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Glad and happy mean the same thing.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'medium', 1, 'What is the opposite of ''open''?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["closed","shut"]'::jsonb, 'If a door is not open, it is closed or shut.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'medium', 1, '''The road was wet and slippery.'' What does ''slippery'' mean?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"easy to slide on"},{"id":"b","text":"very dry"},{"id":"c","text":"very long"},{"id":"d","text":"very hot"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A wet road is easy to slip and slide on. That is what slippery means.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'medium', 1, 'Which words tell how something sounds? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"loud"},{"id":"b","text":"quiet"},{"id":"c","text":"green"},{"id":"d","text":"noisy"},{"id":"e","text":"tall"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Loud, quiet and noisy tell about sounds. Green is a colour and tall is a size.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'hard', 1, 'Put these in order from smallest to biggest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"raindrop"},{"id":"b","text":"puddle"},{"id":"c","text":"pond"},{"id":"d","text":"sea"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A raindrop is tiny. A puddle is bigger, a pond is bigger again, and the sea is the biggest.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'hard', 1, 'Which word means ''very big''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"huge"},{"id":"b","text":"little"},{"id":"c","text":"quick"},{"id":"d","text":"thin"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Huge means very, very big.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'hard', 1, '''Begin'' and ''start'' mean the same thing.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'When you begin something, you start it. They mean the same.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_hard', 1, '''Ben gobbled his lunch and was finished in a minute.'' What does ''gobbled'' mean?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"ate very fast"},{"id":"b","text":"ate very slowly"},{"id":"c","text":"threw away"},{"id":"d","text":"shared"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Ben finished in a minute, so he must have eaten very fast. That is what gobbled means.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which word does NOT belong?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"sock"},{"id":"b","text":"shoe"},{"id":"c","text":"hat"},{"id":"d","text":"spoon"}]'::jsonb, '"d"'::jsonb, 'Socks, shoes and hats are things you wear. A spoon is for eating, so it does not belong.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001120130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011201', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which words mean almost the same as ''little''? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"small"},{"id":"b","text":"tiny"},{"id":"c","text":"huge"},{"id":"d","text":"giant"},{"id":"e","text":"heavy"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b"]'::jsonb, 'Small and tiny mean little. Huge and giant mean very big. Heavy is about weight.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_easy', 1, 'What is the cat''s name?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Max"},{"id":"b","text":"Tilly"},{"id":"c","text":"Milly"},{"id":"d","text":"Tom"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''Her name is Tilly.''', NULL, '{"title":"My Cat","text":"I have a cat. Her name is Tilly. Tilly is black and white.\n\nShe likes to sleep on my bed. In the morning she drinks milk. Then she plays with a ball of wool. I love Tilly."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_easy', 1, 'Tilly is black and white.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''Tilly is black and white.''', NULL, '{"title":"My Cat","text":"I have a cat. Her name is Tilly. Tilly is black and white.\n\nShe likes to sleep on my bed. In the morning she drinks milk. Then she plays with a ball of wool. I love Tilly."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_easy', 1, 'Tilly likes to sleep on my ___.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"bed"'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''She likes to sleep on my bed.''', NULL, '{"title":"My Cat","text":"I have a cat. Her name is Tilly. Tilly is black and white.\n\nShe likes to sleep on my bed. In the morning she drinks milk. Then she plays with a ball of wool. I love Tilly."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'easy', 1, 'Who went to the beach with Jack and Mia?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Mum"},{"id":"b","text":"Dad"},{"id":"c","text":"Grandma"},{"id":"d","text":"a friend"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'The first sentence says they went ''with Dad''.', NULL, '{"title":"At the Beach","text":"Jack and Mia went to the beach with Dad. They made a big sandcastle. Mia found a shell. Jack swam in the waves.\n\nAt lunch they ate fish and chips. A seagull tried to take a chip! Dad shooed it away."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'easy', 1, 'What did they do at the beach? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"made a sandcastle"},{"id":"b","text":"swam in the waves"},{"id":"c","text":"flew a kite"},{"id":"d","text":"ate fish and chips"},{"id":"e","text":"rode bikes"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'The text tells us they made a sandcastle, Jack swam and they ate fish and chips. It does not say kites or bikes.', NULL, '{"title":"At the Beach","text":"Jack and Mia went to the beach with Dad. They made a big sandcastle. Mia found a shell. Jack swam in the waves.\n\nAt lunch they ate fish and chips. A seagull tried to take a chip! Dad shooed it away."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'easy', 1, 'What did Mia find?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["shell","a shell"]'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''Mia found a shell.''', NULL, '{"title":"At the Beach","text":"Jack and Mia went to the beach with Dad. They made a big sandcastle. Mia found a shell. Jack swam in the waves.\n\nAt lunch they ate fish and chips. A seagull tried to take a chip! Dad shooed it away."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'medium', 1, 'What do frogs use to catch bugs?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"their tongue"},{"id":"b","text":"their tail"},{"id":"c","text":"their feet"},{"id":"d","text":"a net"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The text says they catch bugs ''with a long, sticky tongue''.', NULL, '{"title":"Frogs","text":"Frogs live near ponds and creeks. They have long back legs for jumping.\n\nFrogs eat flies and other bugs. They catch them with a long, sticky tongue.\n\nBaby frogs are called tadpoles. Tadpoles live in water and have tails."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'medium', 1, 'Baby frogs are called tadpoles.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''Baby frogs are called tadpoles.''', NULL, '{"title":"Frogs","text":"Frogs live near ponds and creeks. They have long back legs for jumping.\n\nFrogs eat flies and other bugs. They catch them with a long, sticky tongue.\n\nBaby frogs are called tadpoles. Tadpoles live in water and have tails."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'medium', 1, 'Frogs have long back legs. What are they good for?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["jumping","jump","to jump","hopping","hop"]'::jsonb, 'The text says frogs ''have long back legs for jumping''.', NULL, '{"title":"Frogs","text":"Frogs live near ponds and creeks. They have long back legs for jumping.\n\nFrogs eat flies and other bugs. They catch them with a long, sticky tongue.\n\nBaby frogs are called tadpoles. Tadpoles live in water and have tails."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'hard', 1, 'Why could Ella not play outside?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"It was raining."},{"id":"b","text":"It was night."},{"id":"c","text":"She was sick."},{"id":"d","text":"Grandma said no."}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''It was raining, so Ella could not play outside.''', NULL, '{"title":"The Rainy Day","text":"It was raining, so Ella could not play outside. She felt sad.\n\nThen Grandma had an idea. They got out paper, glue and paint. Ella made a picture of a rainbow.\n\nWhen the rain stopped, a real rainbow was in the sky! Ella smiled."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'hard', 1, 'How did Ella feel at the end?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"happy"},{"id":"b","text":"sad"},{"id":"c","text":"angry"},{"id":"d","text":"scared"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'At the end Ella smiled. People smile when they are happy.', NULL, '{"title":"The Rainy Day","text":"It was raining, so Ella could not play outside. She felt sad.\n\nThen Grandma had an idea. They got out paper, glue and paint. Ella made a picture of a rainbow.\n\nWhen the rain stopped, a real rainbow was in the sky! Ella smiled."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'hard', 1, 'Put these in the order they happened.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"It was raining."},{"id":"b","text":"Grandma had an idea."},{"id":"c","text":"Ella made a picture."},{"id":"d","text":"A real rainbow came out."}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'First it rained. Then Grandma had an idea and Ella made a picture. Last, a real rainbow came out.', NULL, '{"title":"The Rainy Day","text":"It was raining, so Ella could not play outside. She felt sad.\n\nThen Grandma had an idea. They got out paper, glue and paint. Ella made a picture of a rainbow.\n\nWhen the rain stopped, a real rainbow was in the sky! Ella smiled."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_hard', 1, 'Who took Leo''s shoe?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Mum"},{"id":"b","text":"Max the puppy"},{"id":"c","text":"Leo''s sister"},{"id":"d","text":"the bus driver"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Max was chewing something black, and Leo cried, ''My shoe!'' So Max had taken it.', NULL, '{"title":"The Lost Shoe","text":"Leo could not find his school shoe. He looked under his bed. He looked in the bath.\n\n“Hurry, Leo, the bus is coming!” called Mum.\n\nThen Leo saw Max, his puppy, in the garden. Max was chewing something black.\n\n“My shoe!” cried Leo."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_hard', 1, 'Where was Leo going?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"to school"},{"id":"b","text":"to the beach"},{"id":"c","text":"to bed"},{"id":"d","text":"to the shops"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'He was looking for his school shoe and the bus was coming, so he was going to school.', NULL, '{"title":"The Lost Shoe","text":"Leo could not find his school shoe. He looked under his bed. He looked in the bath.\n\n“Hurry, Leo, the bus is coming!” called Mum.\n\nThen Leo saw Max, his puppy, in the garden. Max was chewing something black.\n\n“My shoe!” cried Leo."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_hard', 1, 'Leo''s shoe is black.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Max was chewing something black, and Leo saw it was his shoe. So the shoe is black.', NULL, '{"title":"The Lost Shoe","text":"Leo could not find his school shoe. He looked under his bed. He looked in the bath.\n\n“Hurry, Leo, the bus is coming!” called Mum.\n\nThen Leo saw Max, his puppy, in the garden. Max was chewing something black.\n\n“My shoe!” cried Leo."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_easy', 1, 'What colour is Sam''s bike?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"red"},{"id":"b","text":"blue"},{"id":"c","text":"green"},{"id":"d","text":"pink"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''It is blue.''', NULL, '{"title":"My Bike","text":"Sam has a new bike. It is blue. It has a bell that goes ring, ring!\n\nSam rides his bike to the park with his big sister. He wears a helmet to keep his head safe."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_easy', 1, 'Sam wears a ___ to keep his head safe.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"helmet"'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''He wears a helmet to keep his head safe.''', NULL, '{"title":"My Bike","text":"Sam has a new bike. It is blue. It has a bell that goes ring, ring!\n\nSam rides his bike to the park with his big sister. He wears a helmet to keep his head safe."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_easy', 1, 'Sam rides to the park with his big sister.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The text says he rides ''to the park with his big sister''.', NULL, '{"title":"My Bike","text":"Sam has a new bike. It is blue. It has a bell that goes ring, ring!\n\nSam rides his bike to the park with his big sister. He wears a helmet to keep his head safe."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'easy', 1, 'What day was the picnic?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"Sunday"'::jsonb, 'The first words are, ''On Sunday''.', NULL, '{"title":"The Picnic","text":"On Sunday, Ruby and her family had a picnic in the park. They sat on a big rug under a tree.\n\nThey ate sandwiches, apples and cake. Ruby''s brother kicked a ball. Ruby fed bread to the ducks. Then it was time to go home."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'easy', 1, 'What did they eat? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"sandwiches"},{"id":"b","text":"apples"},{"id":"c","text":"pizza"},{"id":"d","text":"cake"},{"id":"e","text":"ice cream"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''They ate sandwiches, apples and cake.''', NULL, '{"title":"The Picnic","text":"On Sunday, Ruby and her family had a picnic in the park. They sat on a big rug under a tree.\n\nThey ate sandwiches, apples and cake. Ruby''s brother kicked a ball. Ruby fed bread to the ducks. Then it was time to go home."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'easy', 1, 'What did Ruby feed to the ducks?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"bread"},{"id":"b","text":"cake"},{"id":"c","text":"apples"},{"id":"d","text":"grass"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''Ruby fed bread to the ducks.''', NULL, '{"title":"The Picnic","text":"On Sunday, Ruby and her family had a picnic in the park. They sat on a big rug under a tree.\n\nThey ate sandwiches, apples and cake. Ruby''s brother kicked a ball. Ruby fed bread to the ducks. Then it was time to go home."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'medium', 1, 'What do kangaroos eat?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"grass"},{"id":"b","text":"fish"},{"id":"c","text":"bugs"},{"id":"d","text":"meat"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''Kangaroos eat grass.''', NULL, '{"title":"Kangaroos","text":"Kangaroos live in Australia. They hop on their strong back legs. They use their long tail to help them balance.\n\nKangaroos eat grass. A mother kangaroo carries her baby in a pouch. The baby is called a joey."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'medium', 1, 'Kangaroos use their tail to help them balance.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The text says they ''use their long tail to help them balance''.', NULL, '{"title":"Kangaroos","text":"Kangaroos live in Australia. They hop on their strong back legs. They use their long tail to help them balance.\n\nKangaroos eat grass. A mother kangaroo carries her baby in a pouch. The baby is called a joey."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'medium', 1, 'Where does a mother kangaroo carry her baby?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["pouch","in a pouch","in her pouch","a pouch","her pouch"]'::jsonb, 'The text says, ''A mother kangaroo carries her baby in a pouch.''', NULL, '{"title":"Kangaroos","text":"Kangaroos live in Australia. They hop on their strong back legs. They use their long tail to help them balance.\n\nKangaroos eat grass. A mother kangaroo carries her baby in a pouch. The baby is called a joey."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'hard', 1, 'What made Ollie''s tooth come out?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"a crunchy apple"},{"id":"b","text":"his toast"},{"id":"c","text":"his pillow"},{"id":"d","text":"a shiny coin"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'He bit into a crunchy apple, then ''Crack! The tooth came out.''', NULL, '{"title":"Ollie''s Tooth","text":"Ollie''s front tooth was wobbly. It wiggled when he ate his toast.\n\nAt lunch, he bit into a crunchy apple. Crack! The tooth came out.\n\nOllie put it in a little box. That night, he put the box under his pillow. In the morning, there was a shiny coin."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'hard', 1, 'Put these in the order they happened.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"The tooth wiggled."},{"id":"b","text":"Ollie bit an apple."},{"id":"c","text":"The tooth came out."},{"id":"d","text":"Ollie found a coin."}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'First the tooth wiggled. Then he bit the apple and the tooth came out. Last, he found a coin in the morning.', NULL, '{"title":"Ollie''s Tooth","text":"Ollie''s front tooth was wobbly. It wiggled when he ate his toast.\n\nAt lunch, he bit into a crunchy apple. Crack! The tooth came out.\n\nOllie put it in a little box. That night, he put the box under his pillow. In the morning, there was a shiny coin."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'hard', 1, 'Why did Ollie put the box under his pillow?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"for the tooth fairy"},{"id":"b","text":"to keep it warm"},{"id":"c","text":"because he was sad"},{"id":"d","text":"to hide it from his dog"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'In the morning there was a coin. The tooth fairy leaves a coin for a tooth under a pillow.', NULL, '{"title":"Ollie''s Tooth","text":"Ollie''s front tooth was wobbly. It wiggled when he ate his toast.\n\nAt lunch, he bit into a crunchy apple. Crack! The tooth came out.\n\nOllie put it in a little box. That night, he put the box under his pillow. In the morning, there was a shiny coin."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_hard', 1, 'How did Pip feel in the storm?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"scared"},{"id":"b","text":"happy"},{"id":"c","text":"hungry"},{"id":"d","text":"sleepy"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Pip hid under the table and shook. That is what a scared dog does.', NULL, '{"title":"The Big Storm","text":"Dark clouds filled the sky. The wind blew the trees. Rain banged on the roof.\n\nNina''s dog, Pip, hid under the table and shook. Nina sat next to him and stroked his ears. “It''s OK, Pip,” she said softly.\n\nSoon the rain stopped and the sun came out. Pip wagged his tail."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which things tell you there was a storm? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"dark clouds"},{"id":"b","text":"the wind blew"},{"id":"c","text":"the sun came out"},{"id":"d","text":"rain banged on the roof"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Dark clouds, wind and heavy rain are signs of a storm. The sun came out after the storm.', NULL, '{"title":"The Big Storm","text":"Dark clouds filled the sky. The wind blew the trees. Rain banged on the roof.\n\nNina''s dog, Pip, hid under the table and shook. Nina sat next to him and stroked his ears. “It''s OK, Pip,” she said softly.\n\nSoon the rain stopped and the sun came out. Pip wagged his tail."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011301', 'very_hard', 1, 'At the end, Pip felt happy again.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Pip wagged his tail. Dogs wag their tails when they are happy.', NULL, '{"title":"The Big Storm","text":"Dark clouds filled the sky. The wind blew the trees. Rain banged on the roof.\n\nNina''s dog, Pip, hid under the table and shook. Nina sat next to him and stroked his ears. “It''s OK, Pip,” she said softly.\n\nSoon the rain stopped and the sun came out. Pip wagged his tail."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130201', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_easy', 1, 'What is the poem about?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"rain"},{"id":"b","text":"snow"},{"id":"c","text":"the sun"},{"id":"d","text":"a cat"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The poem talks about rain falling and puddles.', NULL, '{"title":"Rain","text":"Pitter, patter, on the roof,\nRain is falling, here''s the proof.\n\nPuddles grow along the lane,\nSplish and splash, I love the rain!\n\nBoots are on and so''s my coat,\nNow I''ll sail my paper boat."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130202', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which word rhymes with ''coat'' in the poem?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"boots"},{"id":"b","text":"boat"},{"id":"c","text":"rain"},{"id":"d","text":"roof"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Coat and boat both end in -oat, so they rhyme.', NULL, '{"title":"Rain","text":"Pitter, patter, on the roof,\nRain is falling, here''s the proof.\n\nPuddles grow along the lane,\nSplish and splash, I love the rain!\n\nBoots are on and so''s my coat,\nNow I''ll sail my paper boat."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130203', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_easy', 1, 'The child in the poem likes the rain.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The poem says, ''I love the rain!''', NULL, '{"title":"Rain","text":"Pitter, patter, on the roof,\nRain is falling, here''s the proof.\n\nPuddles grow along the lane,\nSplish and splash, I love the rain!\n\nBoots are on and so''s my coat,\nNow I''ll sail my paper boat."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130204', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'easy', 1, 'Where is the story set?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"at a school"},{"id":"b","text":"at the beach"},{"id":"c","text":"at home"},{"id":"d","text":"at a farm"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It was Zara''s first day at a new school. That is the setting.', NULL, '{"title":"The New Girl","text":"It was Zara''s first day at a new school. She stood by the gate and held Mum''s hand tight. Her tummy felt funny.\n\nThen a girl with a big smile ran over. “Hi, I''m Lily. Do you want to play?”\n\nZara nodded. By lunch, they were best friends."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130205', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'easy', 1, 'How did Zara feel at the start?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"worried"},{"id":"b","text":"angry"},{"id":"c","text":"silly"},{"id":"d","text":"sleepy"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'She held Mum''s hand tight and her tummy felt funny. She was worried about her new school.', NULL, '{"title":"The New Girl","text":"It was Zara''s first day at a new school. She stood by the gate and held Mum''s hand tight. Her tummy felt funny.\n\nThen a girl with a big smile ran over. “Hi, I''m Lily. Do you want to play?”\n\nZara nodded. By lunch, they were best friends."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130206', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'easy', 1, 'What is the name of the girl who said hi?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"Lily"'::jsonb, 'The girl said, ''Hi, I''m Lily.''', NULL, '{"title":"The New Girl","text":"It was Zara''s first day at a new school. She stood by the gate and held Mum''s hand tight. Her tummy felt funny.\n\nThen a girl with a big smile ran over. “Hi, I''m Lily. Do you want to play?”\n\nZara nodded. By lunch, they were best friends."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130207', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'medium', 1, 'Who are the characters in the story? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"Wombat"},{"id":"b","text":"Possum"},{"id":"c","text":"Koala"},{"id":"d","text":"Emu"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b"]'::jsonb, 'Wombat and Possum are in the story. Koala and Emu are not.', NULL, '{"title":"Wombat''s Hole","text":"Wombat dug a hole under the old gum tree. It was cosy and dark.\n\nOne night, a storm came. Possum was wet and cold. “Can I come in?” asked Possum.\n\n“Yes,” said Wombat. “There is room for two.”\n\nThey slept snug and warm until morning."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130208', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'medium', 1, 'What kind of friend is Wombat?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"kind"},{"id":"b","text":"mean"},{"id":"c","text":"lazy"},{"id":"d","text":"scared"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Wombat let wet, cold Possum into the hole. That is a kind thing to do.', NULL, '{"title":"Wombat''s Hole","text":"Wombat dug a hole under the old gum tree. It was cosy and dark.\n\nOne night, a storm came. Possum was wet and cold. “Can I come in?” asked Possum.\n\n“Yes,” said Wombat. “There is room for two.”\n\nThey slept snug and warm until morning."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130209', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'medium', 1, 'Put these in the order they happened.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"Wombat dug a hole."},{"id":"b","text":"A storm came."},{"id":"c","text":"Possum asked to come in."},{"id":"d","text":"They slept until morning."}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'First Wombat dug a hole. Then the storm came and Possum asked to come in. Last, they slept until morning.', NULL, '{"title":"Wombat''s Hole","text":"Wombat dug a hole under the old gum tree. It was cosy and dark.\n\nOne night, a storm came. Possum was wet and cold. “Can I come in?” asked Possum.\n\n“Yes,” said Wombat. “There is room for two.”\n\nThey slept snug and warm until morning."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130210', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'hard', 1, 'Which word rhymes with ''face'' in the poem?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"place"},{"id":"b","text":"round"},{"id":"c","text":"small"},{"id":"d","text":"yard"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Face and place both end in -ace, so they rhyme.', NULL, '{"title":"My Puppy","text":"My puppy is small,\nMy puppy is brown,\nHe runs round the yard\nAnd he jumps up and down.\n\nHe chews on my slipper,\nHe licks at my face,\nHe follows me round\nAll over the place."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130211', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'hard', 1, 'What does the puppy do? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"runs round the yard"},{"id":"b","text":"chews a slipper"},{"id":"c","text":"sings a song"},{"id":"d","text":"licks a face"},{"id":"e","text":"reads a book"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'The poem says he runs round the yard, chews a slipper and licks a face. Puppies cannot sing or read!', NULL, '{"title":"My Puppy","text":"My puppy is small,\nMy puppy is brown,\nHe runs round the yard\nAnd he jumps up and down.\n\nHe chews on my slipper,\nHe licks at my face,\nHe follows me round\nAll over the place."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130212', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'hard', 1, 'The puppy in the poem is big and black.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'The poem says, ''My puppy is small, my puppy is brown.''', NULL, '{"title":"My Puppy","text":"My puppy is small,\nMy puppy is brown,\nHe runs round the yard\nAnd he jumps up and down.\n\nHe chews on my slipper,\nHe licks at my face,\nHe follows me round\nAll over the place."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130213', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_hard', 1, 'What is the problem in the story?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"The string broke and the kite flew away."},{"id":"b","text":"Noah lost his hat."},{"id":"c","text":"It started to rain."},{"id":"d","text":"Dad was sick."}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The problem is what goes wrong. The string broke and the kite was gone.', NULL, '{"title":"The Kite","text":"Noah made a kite with Dad. It was red with a long tail. At the park, the wind lifted it high.\n\nThen, snap! The string broke. The kite flew over the trees and was gone. Noah''s lip wobbled.\n\nDad gave him a hug. “Let''s make another one,” he said. “This time, we''ll make it even better.”"}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130214', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_hard', 1, 'Noah''s lip wobbled. How did he feel?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"sad"},{"id":"b","text":"happy"},{"id":"c","text":"excited"},{"id":"d","text":"proud"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'When your lip wobbles, you feel like crying. Noah was sad that his kite was gone.', NULL, '{"title":"The Kite","text":"Noah made a kite with Dad. It was red with a long tail. At the park, the wind lifted it high.\n\nThen, snap! The string broke. The kite flew over the trees and was gone. Noah''s lip wobbled.\n\nDad gave him a hug. “Let''s make another one,” he said. “This time, we''ll make it even better.”"}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130215', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_hard', 1, 'Dad was cross with Noah.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'Dad gave Noah a hug and wanted to make a new kite. He was kind, not cross.', NULL, '{"title":"The Kite","text":"Noah made a kite with Dad. It was red with a long tail. At the park, the wind lifted it high.\n\nThen, snap! The string broke. The kite flew over the trees and was gone. Noah''s lip wobbled.\n\nDad gave him a hug. “Let''s make another one,” he said. “This time, we''ll make it even better.”"}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130216', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which word rhymes with ''bright''?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"night"},{"id":"b","text":"moon"},{"id":"c","text":"round"},{"id":"d","text":"stars"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Bright and night both end in -ight, so they rhyme.', NULL, '{"title":"The Moon","text":"The moon is round,\nThe moon is bright,\nIt shines on you and me\nAll through the night.\n\nThe stars come out\nTo say hello,\nThey twinkle, twinkle\nSoft and low."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130217', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_easy', 1, 'The poem is about the sun.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'The poem is about the moon and the stars at night.', NULL, '{"title":"The Moon","text":"The moon is round,\nThe moon is bright,\nIt shines on you and me\nAll through the night.\n\nThe stars come out\nTo say hello,\nThey twinkle, twinkle\nSoft and low."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130218', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_easy', 1, 'The moon is round, the moon is ___.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"bright"'::jsonb, 'The poem says, ''The moon is round, the moon is bright.''', NULL, '{"title":"The Moon","text":"The moon is round,\nThe moon is bright,\nIt shines on you and me\nAll through the night.\n\nThe stars come out\nTo say hello,\nThey twinkle, twinkle\nSoft and low."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130219', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'easy', 1, 'How old was Tom?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["6","six"]'::jsonb, 'The story says, ''He was six!''', NULL, '{"title":"Tom''s Birthday","text":"Today was Tom''s birthday. He was six! Mum made a chocolate cake with six candles.\n\nAll his friends came to the party. They played games in the backyard. Tom blew out the candles and made a wish.\n\nIt was the best day ever."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130220', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'easy', 1, 'Where did they play games?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"in the backyard"},{"id":"b","text":"at the beach"},{"id":"c","text":"at school"},{"id":"d","text":"in the car"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The story says, ''They played games in the backyard.''', NULL, '{"title":"Tom''s Birthday","text":"Today was Tom''s birthday. He was six! Mum made a chocolate cake with six candles.\n\nAll his friends came to the party. They played games in the backyard. Tom blew out the candles and made a wish.\n\nIt was the best day ever."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130221', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'easy', 1, 'How did Tom feel on his birthday?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"happy"},{"id":"b","text":"sad"},{"id":"c","text":"scared"},{"id":"d","text":"angry"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Tom said it was the best day ever, so he felt happy.', NULL, '{"title":"Tom''s Birthday","text":"Today was Tom''s birthday. He was six! Mum made a chocolate cake with six candles.\n\nAll his friends came to the party. They played games in the backyard. Tom blew out the candles and made a wish.\n\nIt was the best day ever."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130222', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'medium', 1, 'Who is the main character?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Maggie the magpie"},{"id":"b","text":"the cat"},{"id":"c","text":"the worm"},{"id":"d","text":"the gum tree"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The story is mostly about Maggie the magpie and what she does.', NULL, '{"title":"The Hungry Magpie","text":"Maggie the magpie was hungry. She saw a worm in the grass.\n\nShe swooped down, but a cat was hiding behind the bush! Maggie flew up into the gum tree just in time.\n\nThe cat looked up and licked its lips. Maggie stayed in the tree until the cat went away."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130223', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'medium', 1, 'Put these in the order they happened.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"Maggie saw a worm."},{"id":"b","text":"Maggie swooped down."},{"id":"c","text":"Maggie flew into the tree."},{"id":"d","text":"The cat went away."}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'First Maggie saw a worm and swooped down. Then she flew into the tree. Last, the cat went away.', NULL, '{"title":"The Hungry Magpie","text":"Maggie the magpie was hungry. She saw a worm in the grass.\n\nShe swooped down, but a cat was hiding behind the bush! Maggie flew up into the gum tree just in time.\n\nThe cat looked up and licked its lips. Maggie stayed in the tree until the cat went away."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130224', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'medium', 1, 'The cat caught Maggie.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'Maggie flew up into the gum tree just in time, so the cat did not catch her.', NULL, '{"title":"The Hungry Magpie","text":"Maggie the magpie was hungry. She saw a worm in the grass.\n\nShe swooped down, but a cat was hiding behind the bush! Maggie flew up into the gum tree just in time.\n\nThe cat looked up and licked its lips. Maggie stayed in the tree until the cat went away."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130225', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'hard', 1, 'Which animals are in the poem? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"cow"},{"id":"b","text":"sheep"},{"id":"c","text":"horse"},{"id":"d","text":"hen"},{"id":"e","text":"pig"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'The poem has a cow, a sheep, a dog and a hen. There is no horse or pig.', NULL, '{"title":"At the Farm","text":"The cow says moo,\nThe sheep says baa,\nThe dog barks loud\nAt Grandpa''s car.\n\nThe hen lays eggs\nUp in the shed,\nAnd when it''s dark\nWe go to bed."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130226', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'hard', 1, 'Where is the poem set?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"on a farm"},{"id":"b","text":"at the beach"},{"id":"c","text":"in a city"},{"id":"d","text":"at school"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The poem has cows, sheep, hens and a shed. It is set on a farm.', NULL, '{"title":"At the Farm","text":"The cow says moo,\nThe sheep says baa,\nThe dog barks loud\nAt Grandpa''s car.\n\nThe hen lays eggs\nUp in the shed,\nAnd when it''s dark\nWe go to bed."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130227', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'hard', 1, 'Which word in the poem rhymes with ''shed''?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"bed"'::jsonb, 'Shed and bed both end in -ed, so they rhyme.', NULL, '{"title":"At the Farm","text":"The cow says moo,\nThe sheep says baa,\nThe dog barks loud\nAt Grandpa''s car.\n\nThe hen lays eggs\nUp in the shed,\nAnd when it''s dark\nWe go to bed."}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130228', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_hard', 1, 'How did Ava''s feelings change?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"scared at first, then not scared"},{"id":"b","text":"happy at first, then scared"},{"id":"c","text":"angry the whole time"},{"id":"d","text":"sad at first, then angry"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'At first Ava screamed and ran, so she was scared. At the end she waved goodbye, so she was not scared any more.', NULL, '{"title":"Ava and the Spider","text":"Ava saw a big, hairy spider on the wall. She screamed and ran to get Dad.\n\nDad caught the spider in a jar. “It won''t hurt you,” he said. “It eats flies.”\n\nAva looked closely. The spider had eight long legs. Dad let it go in the garden. Ava waved. “Bye, spider!”"}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130229', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_hard', 1, 'Dad hurt the spider.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'Dad caught it in a jar and let it go in the garden. He did not hurt it.', NULL, '{"title":"Ava and the Spider","text":"Ava saw a big, hairy spider on the wall. She screamed and ran to get Dad.\n\nDad caught the spider in a jar. “It won''t hurt you,” he said. “It eats flies.”\n\nAva looked closely. The spider had eight long legs. Dad let it go in the garden. Ava waved. “Bye, spider!”"}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001130230', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011302', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which words describe the spider? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"big"},{"id":"b","text":"hairy"},{"id":"c","text":"tiny"},{"id":"d","text":"green"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b"]'::jsonb, 'The story says it was a ''big, hairy spider''. It does not say tiny or green.', NULL, '{"title":"Ava and the Spider","text":"Ava saw a big, hairy spider on the wall. She screamed and ran to get Dad.\n\nDad caught the spider in a jar. “It won''t hurt you,” he said. “It eats flies.”\n\nAva looked closely. The spider had eight long legs. Dad let it go in the garden. Ava waved. “Bye, spider!”"}'::jsonb, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which sentence starts with a capital letter?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the dog ran."},{"id":"b","text":"The dog ran."},{"id":"c","text":"the Dog ran."},{"id":"d","text":"tHe dog ran."}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'A sentence starts with a capital letter. ''The'' has a capital T.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_easy', 1, 'A telling sentence ends with a full stop.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A sentence that tells us something ends with a full stop (.).', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_easy', 1, 'What goes at the end of this sentence? ''I like apples''', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"."},{"id":"b","text":"?"},{"id":"c","text":","}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It tells us something. It is not a question, so it ends with a full stop.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'easy', 1, 'Which one is a question?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Where is my hat?"},{"id":"b","text":"My hat is red."},{"id":"c","text":"I have a hat."},{"id":"d","text":"The hat is big."}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A question asks something and ends with a question mark (?). ''Where is my hat?'' asks something.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'easy', 1, 'Use ''and'' or ''but''. I have a cat ___ a dog.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"and"'::jsonb, 'I have both pets, so we join them with ''and''.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'easy', 1, 'Which words always need a capital letter? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"sydney"},{"id":"b","text":"tom"},{"id":"c","text":"dog"},{"id":"d","text":"monday"},{"id":"e","text":"ball"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Names of places, people and days need a capital letter: Sydney, Tom, Monday.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'medium', 1, 'Put the words in order to make a sentence.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"My"},{"id":"b","text":"dog"},{"id":"c","text":"likes"},{"id":"d","text":"bones."}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, '''My'' has a capital letter, so it goes first. ''bones.'' has the full stop, so it goes last: My dog likes bones.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'medium', 1, 'Which joining word fits? ''I wanted to play outside, ___ it was raining.''', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"and"},{"id":"b","text":"but"},{"id":"c","text":"so"},{"id":"d","text":"or"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'The second part tells us something that stopped the first. We use ''but'' for that.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'medium', 1, 'This sentence has its capital letter right: ''i went to the park.''', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'The word ''I'' is always a capital letter, and a sentence must start with a capital: I went to the park.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'hard', 1, 'Which sentence is written correctly?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"we went to bondi beach."},{"id":"b","text":"We went to Bondi Beach."},{"id":"c","text":"We went to bondi beach"},{"id":"d","text":"we Went to Bondi beach."}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Start with a capital letter, give the place name capitals (Bondi Beach) and end with a full stop.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'hard', 1, 'Join with ''but''. I am tall. My brother is short. I am tall ___ my brother is short.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"but"'::jsonb, 'Tall and short are different, so we join them with ''but''.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'hard', 1, 'Which of these need a question mark? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"Do you like cake"},{"id":"b","text":"I like cake"},{"id":"c","text":"Where is Mum"},{"id":"d","text":"Who is that"},{"id":"e","text":"Mum is home"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c","d"]'::jsonb, '''Do you like cake'', ''Where is Mum'' and ''Who is that'' ask something, so they need a question mark.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_hard', 1, 'Put the words in order to make a question.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"Can"},{"id":"b","text":"you"},{"id":"c","text":"see"},{"id":"d","text":"the"},{"id":"e","text":"bird?"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d","e"]'::jsonb, '''Can'' has a capital letter, so it starts. ''bird?'' has the question mark, so it ends: Can you see the bird?', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which sentence is fully correct?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"is it time for lunch?"},{"id":"b","text":"Is it time for lunch."},{"id":"c","text":"Is it time for lunch?"},{"id":"d","text":"is it time for lunch."}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, 'It needs a capital letter at the start. It asks something, so it ends with a question mark.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which is the right way to write this? ''my friend sam likes footy''', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"My friend Sam likes footy."},{"id":"b","text":"my friend Sam likes footy."},{"id":"c","text":"My friend sam likes footy"},{"id":"d","text":"My Friend Sam Likes Footy."}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Start with a capital (My), give the name a capital (Sam) and end with a full stop.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_easy', 1, 'Every sentence starts with a capital letter.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Yes. The first word of a sentence always starts with a capital letter.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which one is a sentence?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"The sun is hot."},{"id":"b","text":"sun hot the"},{"id":"c","text":"is the hot"},{"id":"d","text":"hot sun the"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '''The sun is hot.'' makes sense, starts with a capital and ends with a full stop.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_easy', 1, 'What goes at the end of this question? ''Are you hungry''', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"?"},{"id":"b","text":"."},{"id":"c","text":","}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It asks something, so it ends with a question mark.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'easy', 1, 'Which word needs a capital letter? ''my dog is big.''', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"my"},{"id":"b","text":"dog"},{"id":"c","text":"is"},{"id":"d","text":"big"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '''my'' is the first word of the sentence, so it needs a capital: My dog is big.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'easy', 1, 'Use ''and'' or ''but''. I am hungry ___ there is no food.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"but"'::jsonb, 'The second part is a problem for the first part, so we join them with ''but''.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'easy', 1, '''Where is the bus?'' is a question.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'It asks something and ends with a question mark, so it is a question.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'medium', 1, 'Which words always need a capital letter? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"emma"},{"id":"b","text":"chair"},{"id":"c","text":"perth"},{"id":"d","text":"friday"},{"id":"e","text":"apple"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'Names of people, places and days need capitals: Emma, Perth, Friday.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'medium', 1, 'Put the words in order to make a sentence.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"We"},{"id":"b","text":"play"},{"id":"c","text":"at"},{"id":"d","text":"school."}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, '''We'' has a capital letter, so it goes first. ''school.'' has the full stop, so it goes last: We play at school.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'medium', 1, 'Which joining word fits? ''I like dogs ___ I like cats.''', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"and"},{"id":"b","text":"but"},{"id":"c","text":"is"},{"id":"d","text":"the"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'I like both, so we join them with ''and''.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'hard', 1, 'Which sentence is written correctly?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"my nan lives in Dubbo."},{"id":"b","text":"My nan lives in Dubbo."},{"id":"c","text":"My nan lives in dubbo."},{"id":"d","text":"my nan lives in dubbo"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Start with a capital (My), give the town a capital (Dubbo) and end with a full stop.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'hard', 1, 'Join with ''and''. Ben has a ball. Ben has a bat. Ben has a ball ___ a bat.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"and"'::jsonb, 'Ben has both things, so we join them with ''and''.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'hard', 1, 'Which sentence has the full stop in the right place?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"I see a. bird"},{"id":"b","text":"I see a bird."},{"id":"c","text":".I see a bird"},{"id":"d","text":"I see. a bird"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'The full stop goes at the very end of the sentence: I see a bird.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_hard', 1, 'Put these sentences in order to tell about the morning.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"I got out of bed."},{"id":"b","text":"I ate my breakfast."},{"id":"c","text":"I went to school."}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'First you get out of bed. Then you eat breakfast. Last, you go to school.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which sentences are written correctly? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"Lucy has a red bike."},{"id":"b","text":"lucy has a red bike."},{"id":"c","text":"Can I have a turn?"},{"id":"d","text":"can I have a turn."},{"id":"e","text":"My cat is black"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c"]'::jsonb, 'Correct sentences start with a capital and end with a full stop or question mark. The others miss one of these.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000001140130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000011401', 'very_hard', 1, 'How many sentences are here? ''I have a dog. His name is Rex. He is funny.''', 'short_answer', NULL, '["3","three"]'::jsonb, 'Count the full stops. Each sentence ends with one, and there are three.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_easy', 1, 'What number do these blocks show?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"47"'::jsonb, 'There are 4 tens and 7 ones. 40 and 7 make 47.', '{"kind":"blocks","hundreds":0,"tens":4,"ones":7}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_easy', 1, 'What is the value of the 3 in 35?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"3"},{"id":"b","text":"30"},{"id":"c","text":"300"},{"id":"d","text":"35"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'The 3 is in the tens place. It is worth 3 tens, or 30.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_easy', 1, 'In 208, the 0 shows there are no tens.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, '208 is 2 hundreds, 0 tens and 8 ones. The 0 holds the tens place.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'easy', 1, 'Which number do these blocks show?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"26"},{"id":"b","text":"206"},{"id":"c","text":"260"},{"id":"d","text":"2006"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'There are 2 hundreds, no tens and 6 ones. We write 0 in the tens place: 206.', '{"kind":"blocks","hundreds":2,"tens":0,"ones":6}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'easy', 1, 'Write three hundred and forty-two in numerals.', 'short_answer', NULL, '"342"'::jsonb, '3 hundreds, 4 tens and 2 ones is 342.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'easy', 1, 'Put these numbers in order from smallest to largest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"109"},{"id":"b","text":"190"},{"id":"c","text":"901"},{"id":"d","text":"910"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'Look at the hundreds first. 109 and 190 have 1 hundred. 109 has 0 tens, so it is smaller. Then 901, then 910.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'medium', 1, '573 = 500 + ___ + 3', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"70"'::jsonb, 'The 7 in 573 is in the tens place. It is worth 70.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'medium', 1, 'Which number is three hundred and five?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"35"},{"id":"b","text":"305"},{"id":"c","text":"350"},{"id":"d","text":"3005"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, '3 hundreds, no tens and 5 ones. The 0 holds the tens place: 305.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'medium', 1, 'What number is 10 more than 495?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"505"'::jsonb, '10 more adds 1 ten. 9 tens and 1 more ten is 10 tens, which is 1 hundred. So 495 becomes 505.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'hard', 1, 'Which number is the largest?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"689"},{"id":"b","text":"698"},{"id":"c","text":"869"},{"id":"d","text":"896"}]'::jsonb, '"d"'::jsonb, '869 and 896 both have 8 hundreds. 896 has 9 tens, which is more than 6 tens.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'hard', 1, 'Which numbers have a 0 in the tens place? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"407"},{"id":"b","text":"470"},{"id":"c","text":"802"},{"id":"d","text":"120"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c"]'::jsonb, 'In 407 and 802 the middle digit is 0, so there are no tens. In 470 and 120 the 0 is in the ones place.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'hard', 1, 'What number is 1 more than 699?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"700"'::jsonb, '1 more than 699 fills the ones and the tens. It goes up to 7 hundreds: 700.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_hard', 1, 'What is the largest 3-digit number you can make with the digits 4, 0 and 7? Use each digit once.', 'short_answer', NULL, '"740"'::jsonb, 'Put the biggest digit in the hundreds place, then the next biggest: 7, then 4, then 0. That makes 740.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_hard', 1, 'What is the smallest 3-digit number you can make with the digits 5, 0 and 2? Use each digit once.', 'short_answer', NULL, '"205"'::jsonb, 'A 3-digit number can''t start with 0. Start with 2, then put 0 in the tens and 5 in the ones: 205.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_hard', 1, 'Sam wrote six hundred and nine as 6009. What should he have written?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"609"'::jsonb, 'Six hundred and nine is 6 hundreds, 0 tens and 9 ones. It has 3 digits: 609.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which number do these blocks show?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"26"},{"id":"b","text":"62"},{"id":"c","text":"602"},{"id":"d","text":"8"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'There are 6 tens and 2 ones. 60 and 2 make 62.', '{"kind":"blocks","hundreds":0,"tens":6,"ones":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_easy', 1, 'What number is 1 more than 59?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"60"'::jsonb, '1 more than 9 ones makes a new ten. 5 tens become 6 tens: 60.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_easy', 1, 'In 84, the 8 is worth 80.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The 8 is in the tens place, so it is worth 8 tens, or 80.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'easy', 1, 'What is the value of the 4 in 438?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"4"},{"id":"b","text":"40"},{"id":"c","text":"400"},{"id":"d","text":"438"}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, 'The 4 is in the hundreds place. It is worth 4 hundreds, or 400.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'easy', 1, 'What number do these blocks show?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"310"'::jsonb, '3 hundreds, 1 ten and no ones. Write 0 in the ones place: 310.', '{"kind":"blocks","hundreds":3,"tens":1,"ones":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'easy', 1, '406 and 460 are the same number.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, '406 has 0 tens and 6 ones. 460 has 6 tens and 0 ones. 460 is bigger.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'medium', 1, 'Put these numbers in order from largest to smallest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"752"},{"id":"b","text":"725"},{"id":"c","text":"572"},{"id":"d","text":"527"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, '752 and 725 have 7 hundreds, so they come first. 752 has more tens than 725. Then 572, then 527.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'medium', 1, '800 + 4 = ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"804"'::jsonb, '8 hundreds, no tens and 4 ones. The 0 holds the tens place: 804.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'medium', 1, 'Which number comes just before 300?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"301"},{"id":"b","text":"299"},{"id":"c","text":"290"},{"id":"d","text":"200"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, '1 less than 300 is 299.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'hard', 1, 'The number line goes from 0 to 1000 in 10 equal jumps. What number is the dot on?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"700"'::jsonb, '10 equal jumps to 1000 means each jump is 100. The dot is after 7 jumps: 700.', '{"kind":"number_line","from":0,"to":1000,"jumps":10,"dotAt":7}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'hard', 1, 'Which number is between 590 and 610?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"509"},{"id":"b","text":"601"},{"id":"c","text":"619"},{"id":"d","text":"690"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, '601 is 6 hundreds and 1 one. It is more than 590 and less than 610.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'hard', 1, 'What number is 10 less than 403?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"393"'::jsonb, '403 has no tens, so take 1 hundred and make it 10 tens. 10 less than 403 is 393.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which numbers are bigger than 550 but smaller than 600? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"505"},{"id":"b","text":"559"},{"id":"c","text":"595"},{"id":"d","text":"650"}]'::jsonb, '["b","c"]'::jsonb, '559 and 595 have 5 hundreds and more than 5 tens. 505 is less than 550. 650 is more than 600.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_hard', 1, 'A number has 7 hundreds, 4 ones and no tens. What is the number?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"704"'::jsonb, '7 hundreds, 0 tens and 4 ones is 704.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020101', 'very_hard', 1, 'Put these numbers in order from smallest to largest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"99"},{"id":"b","text":"909"},{"id":"c","text":"990"},{"id":"d","text":"999"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, '99 has only 2 digits, so it is smallest. 909 has 0 tens, 990 has 9 tens and 0 ones, and 999 is largest.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010201', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_easy', 1, 'What do these blocks show?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"5 tens and 3 ones"},{"id":"b","text":"3 tens and 5 ones"},{"id":"c","text":"53 tens"},{"id":"d","text":"8 ones"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'There are 5 long rods (tens) and 3 small cubes (ones).', '{"kind":"blocks","hundreds":0,"tens":5,"ones":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010202', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_easy', 1, '40 + 6 = ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"46"'::jsonb, '4 tens and 6 ones make 46.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010203', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_easy', 1, '10 ones make 1 ten.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'When you have 10 ones, you can swap them for 1 ten.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010204', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'easy', 1, '300 + 20 + 7 = ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"327"'::jsonb, '3 hundreds, 2 tens and 7 ones make 327.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010205', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'easy', 1, 'How many tens are in 60?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'Count by tens: 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60. That is 6 tens.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010206', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'easy', 1, 'Which is the same as 258?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"2 hundreds, 5 tens and 8 ones"},{"id":"b","text":"2 hundreds, 8 tens and 5 ones"},{"id":"c","text":"25 hundreds and 8 ones"},{"id":"d","text":"5 hundreds, 2 tens and 8 ones"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'In 258 the 2 is hundreds, the 5 is tens and the 8 is ones.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010207', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'medium', 1, 'How many tens are in 340?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"34"'::jsonb, '300 is 30 tens and 40 is 4 tens. 30 + 4 = 34 tens.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010208', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'medium', 1, '56 = 40 + ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"16"'::jsonb, '56 is 5 tens and 6 ones. Use 4 tens, and the last ten plus 6 ones is 16.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010209', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'medium', 1, 'Which of these are the same as the number the blocks show? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"125"},{"id":"b","text":"100 + 20 + 5"},{"id":"c","text":"12 tens and 5 ones"},{"id":"d","text":"152"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'The blocks show 1 hundred, 2 tens and 5 ones, which is 125. 1 hundred is 10 tens, so it is also 12 tens and 5 ones. 152 is a different number.', '{"kind":"blocks","hundreds":1,"tens":2,"ones":5}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010210', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'hard', 1, 'How many tens are in 1000?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"100"'::jsonb, '10 tens make 100. 1000 is 10 hundreds, and 10 lots of 10 tens is 100 tens.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010211', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'hard', 1, 'Which number is 4 hundreds and 13 tens?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"413"},{"id":"b","text":"430"},{"id":"c","text":"530"},{"id":"d","text":"4130"}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, '13 tens is 130. 400 + 130 = 530.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010212', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'hard', 1, '620 is 5 hundreds and ___ tens.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"12"'::jsonb, '620 − 500 = 120, and 120 is 12 tens.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010213', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_hard', 1, 'Jack has 23 ten-dollar notes. How many dollars does he have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["230","$230"]'::jsonb, '23 tens is 230. So 23 ten-dollar notes make $230.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010214', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which are ways to make 470? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"47 tens"},{"id":"b","text":"400 + 70"},{"id":"c","text":"3 hundreds and 17 tens"},{"id":"d","text":"4 hundreds and 7 ones"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, '47 tens is 470. 400 + 70 = 470. 300 + 170 = 470. But 4 hundreds and 7 ones is only 407.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010215', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_hard', 1, 'Pencils come in boxes of 10. How many boxes do you need for 350 pencils?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"35"'::jsonb, '350 is 35 tens, so you need 35 boxes of 10.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010216', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_easy', 1, '70 + 3 = ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"73"'::jsonb, '7 tens and 3 ones make 73.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010217', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_easy', 1, 'How many ones make 1 ten?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"1"},{"id":"b","text":"5"},{"id":"c","text":"10"},{"id":"d","text":"100"}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, '10 ones make 1 ten.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010218', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_easy', 1, 'The blocks show 3 tens and 4 ones.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'There are 3 long rods (tens) and 4 small cubes (ones). That is 34.', '{"kind":"blocks","hundreds":0,"tens":3,"ones":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010219', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'easy', 1, 'How many hundreds are in 600?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'Count by hundreds: 100, 200, 300, 400, 500, 600. That is 6 hundreds.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010220', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'easy', 1, '491 = 400 + 90 + ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"1"'::jsonb, '491 is 4 hundreds, 9 tens and 1 one.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010221', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'easy', 1, 'Which shows the number the blocks make?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"200 + 30"},{"id":"b","text":"200 + 3"},{"id":"c","text":"20 + 3"},{"id":"d","text":"300 + 20"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'There are 2 hundreds and 3 tens, with no ones. That is 200 + 30 = 230.', '{"kind":"blocks","hundreds":2,"tens":3,"ones":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010222', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'medium', 1, 'Which number is 7 tens and 15 ones?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"85"},{"id":"b","text":"75"},{"id":"c","text":"715"},{"id":"d","text":"22"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '7 tens is 70. 15 ones is 15. 70 + 15 = 85.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010223', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'medium', 1, '83 = 70 + ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"13"'::jsonb, '83 is 8 tens and 3 ones. Use 7 tens, and the last ten plus 3 ones is 13.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010224', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'medium', 1, 'How many tens are in 250?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"25"'::jsonb, '200 is 20 tens and 50 is 5 tens. 20 + 5 = 25 tens.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010225', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'hard', 1, 'Which are ways to make 36? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"3 tens and 6 ones"},{"id":"b","text":"2 tens and 16 ones"},{"id":"c","text":"1 ten and 26 ones"},{"id":"d","text":"36 tens"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, '30 + 6, 20 + 16 and 10 + 26 all make 36. But 36 tens is 360.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010226', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'hard', 1, '1 hundred is the same as ___ tens.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"10"'::jsonb, 'Count by tens to 100: 10, 20, 30 ... 100. That is 10 tens.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010227', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'hard', 1, 'Which is the same as 900?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"9 tens"},{"id":"b","text":"90 tens"},{"id":"c","text":"90 ones"},{"id":"d","text":"900 tens"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, '1 hundred is 10 tens, so 9 hundreds is 90 tens.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010228', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_hard', 1, '350 is 2 hundreds and ___ tens.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"15"'::jsonb, '350 − 200 = 150, and 150 is 15 tens.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010229', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_hard', 1, 'Ella has 5 hundreds blocks, 14 tens blocks and 3 ones blocks. What number does she have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"643"'::jsonb, '5 hundreds is 500. 14 tens is 140. 500 + 140 + 3 = 643.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002010230', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020102', 'very_hard', 1, 'Put these in order from smallest to largest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"45 tens"},{"id":"b","text":"5 hundreds"},{"id":"c","text":"52 tens"},{"id":"d","text":"6 hundreds and 3 ones"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, '45 tens is 450, 5 hundreds is 500, 52 tens is 520, and 6 hundreds and 3 ones is 603.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_easy', 1, '7 + 3 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"10"'::jsonb, '7 and 3 are a pair that makes 10.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_easy', 1, '6 + ___ = 10', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"4"'::jsonb, '6 and 4 make 10. Count on from 6: 7, 8, 9, 10. That is 4.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_easy', 1, '20 + 30 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"50"'::jsonb, '2 tens and 3 tens make 5 tens, which is 50.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'easy', 1, '24 + 15 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"39"'::jsonb, 'Add the tens: 20 + 10 = 30. Add the ones: 4 + 5 = 9. 30 + 9 = 39.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'easy', 1, '48 − 23 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"25"'::jsonb, 'Take away the tens: 40 − 20 = 20. Take away the ones: 8 − 3 = 5. 20 + 5 = 25.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'easy', 1, 'If 9 + 6 = 15, then 15 − 6 = 9.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Adding and taking away undo each other. 15 take away the 6 gets back to 9.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'medium', 1, '37 + 26 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"63"'::jsonb, 'Add the tens: 30 + 20 = 50. Add the ones: 7 + 6 = 13. 50 + 13 = 63.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'medium', 1, '52 − 18 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"34"'::jsonb, 'Take away 20 to get 32, then add back 2 because you took too many. 32 + 2 = 34.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'medium', 1, 'Lily had 45 stickers. She got 30 more. How many stickers does she have now?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"15"},{"id":"b","text":"75"},{"id":"c","text":"65"},{"id":"d","text":"70"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Getting more means add. 45 + 30: add 3 tens to 4 tens to get 7 tens. 75.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'hard', 1, '16 + 4 = 10 + 10', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Both sides make 20, so they are equal.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'hard', 1, 'Which of these make 100? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"60 + 40"},{"id":"b","text":"75 + 25"},{"id":"c","text":"55 + 55"},{"id":"d","text":"35 + 65"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, '60 + 40, 75 + 25 and 35 + 65 all make 100. 55 + 55 is 110.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'hard', 1, 'A bus had 63 people on it. 27 people got off. How many people are on the bus now?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"36"'::jsonb, '63 − 27: take away 30 to get 33, then add back 3. 33 + 3 = 36.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_hard', 1, '35 + ___ = 20 + 40', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"25"'::jsonb, '20 + 40 = 60. Both sides must be equal, so 35 + ? = 60. 60 − 35 = 25.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_hard', 1, 'Noah has 58 cards. Ruby has 19 more cards than Noah. How many cards does Ruby have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"77"'::jsonb, '19 more means add. 58 + 20 = 78, then take away 1. 77.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_hard', 1, '34 + 48 = 82. Which number sentence is also true?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"82 − 48 = 34"},{"id":"b","text":"48 − 34 = 82"},{"id":"c","text":"34 − 82 = 48"},{"id":"d","text":"82 + 34 = 48"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The big number 82 is the whole. Take away one part (48) and you get the other part (34).', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_easy', 1, '___ + 5 = 10', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, '5 and 5 make 10.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_easy', 1, '15 − 5 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"10"'::jsonb, '15 is 10 and 5. Take away the 5 and 10 is left.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_easy', 1, '3 + 7 = 7 + 3', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'You can add in any order. Both sides make 10.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'easy', 1, '40 + 25 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"65"'::jsonb, 'Add the tens: 40 + 20 = 60. Then add the 5 ones: 65.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'easy', 1, '67 − 30 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"37"'::jsonb, 'Take away 3 tens from 6 tens: 3 tens are left. Keep the 7 ones: 37.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'easy', 1, 'Which pair of numbers makes 20?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"12 and 8"},{"id":"b","text":"11 and 8"},{"id":"c","text":"14 and 7"},{"id":"d","text":"15 and 4"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '12 + 8 = 20. The others make 19, 21 and 19.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'medium', 1, '46 + 38 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"84"'::jsonb, 'Add the tens: 40 + 30 = 70. Add the ones: 6 + 8 = 14. 70 + 14 = 84.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'medium', 1, '71 − 26 = ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"45"'::jsonb, 'Count up from 26: 4 to 30, then 41 to 71. 4 + 41 = 45.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'medium', 1, '90 − ___ = 55', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"35"'::jsonb, 'Count up from 55 to 90: 5 to 60, then 30 to 90. 5 + 30 = 35.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'hard', 1, 'Ben scored 47 runs in cricket. Kai scored 35 runs. How many runs did they score altogether?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"82"'::jsonb, '47 + 35: 40 + 30 = 70 and 7 + 5 = 12. 70 + 12 = 82.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'hard', 1, '50 − 20 = 20 + 20', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, '50 − 20 = 30, but 20 + 20 = 40. The two sides are not equal.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'hard', 1, 'There were 80 people at netball. 45 people went home. How many people stayed?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"35"},{"id":"b","text":"45"},{"id":"c","text":"125"},{"id":"d","text":"25"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '80 − 45: count up from 45. 5 to 50, then 30 to 80. 5 + 30 = 35.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_hard', 1, '64 − ___ = 50 − 10', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"24"'::jsonb, '50 − 10 = 40. So 64 − ? = 40. 64 − 24 = 40.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_hard', 1, 'Zoe had $90. She spent $34 on a book and $25 on a hat. How much money does she have left?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["31","$31"]'::jsonb, 'She spent 34 + 25 = 59 dollars. 90 − 59 = 31, so she has $31 left.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002020130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020201', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which number sentences are true? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"28 + 15 = 43"},{"id":"b","text":"43 − 15 = 28"},{"id":"c","text":"43 − 28 = 15"},{"id":"d","text":"15 − 43 = 28"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, '28 and 15 are the parts and 43 is the whole. 28 + 15 = 43, and taking a part from 43 leaves the other part. 15 − 43 doesn''t work.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_easy', 1, 'Look at the array. How many dots are there altogether?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"10"'::jsonb, 'There are 2 rows of 5 dots. 5, 10. That is 10 dots.', '{"kind":"array","rows":2,"columns":5}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_easy', 1, 'There are 3 plates with 2 apples on each plate. How many apples are there?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"5"},{"id":"b","text":"6"},{"id":"c","text":"8"},{"id":"d","text":"32"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, '3 groups of 2: count by twos. 2, 4, 6.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_easy', 1, '4 groups of 5 make 20.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Count by fives 4 times: 5, 10, 15, 20.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'easy', 1, 'Which matches the array?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"3 rows of 5"},{"id":"b","text":"3 rows of 3"},{"id":"c","text":"5 rows of 5"},{"id":"d","text":"3 + 5"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Count the rows going across: 3. Each row has 5 dots. So it is 3 rows of 5.', '{"kind":"array","rows":3,"columns":5}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'easy', 1, '12 strawberries are shared equally between 2 children. How many does each child get?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'Share them out one at a time. 6 + 6 = 12, so each child gets 6.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'easy', 1, 'Count by tens: 10, 20, 30, ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"40"'::jsonb, 'Each jump adds 10. 30 + 10 = 40.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'medium', 1, 'There are 5 bags with 4 oranges in each bag. How many oranges are there?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"20"'::jsonb, '5 groups of 4: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'medium', 1, 'This array shows 4 rows of 3. It has 12 dots.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'There are 4 rows with 3 dots in each row. 3, 6, 9, 12.', '{"kind":"array","rows":4,"columns":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'medium', 1, '20 children make teams of 5. How many teams are there?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"4"},{"id":"b","text":"5"},{"id":"c","text":"15"},{"id":"d","text":"25"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Count by fives until you reach 20: 5, 10, 15, 20. That is 4 teams.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'hard', 1, 'Which of these are ways to put 12 counters into equal groups? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"2 groups of 6"},{"id":"b","text":"3 groups of 4"},{"id":"c","text":"5 groups of 2"},{"id":"d","text":"4 groups of 3"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, '2 × 6, 3 × 4 and 4 × 3 all make 12. 5 groups of 2 is only 10.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'hard', 1, '15 pencils are shared equally into 3 cups. How many pencils go in each cup?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, 'Share them out: 5 + 5 + 5 = 15, so each cup gets 5.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'hard', 1, 'Each bike has 2 wheels. How many wheels are on 9 bikes?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"18"'::jsonb, '9 groups of 2: count by twos 9 times. 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 18.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_hard', 1, 'Amy has 17 stickers. She puts them in rows of 5. How many full rows can she make?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"3"'::jsonb, '3 rows of 5 is 15. That leaves 2 stickers, which is not enough for another full row.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which of these is NOT true about the array?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"It has 3 rows of 6"},{"id":"b","text":"It has 6 columns of 3"},{"id":"c","text":"It has 18 dots"},{"id":"d","text":"It has 3 rows of 5"}]'::jsonb, '"d"'::jsonb, 'There are 3 rows with 6 dots in each, so 18 dots. You can also see 6 columns of 3. Each row has 6, not 5.', '{"kind":"array","rows":3,"columns":6}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_hard', 1, 'There are 4 tables with 5 children at each table. Then 2 more children come in. How many children are there now?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"22"'::jsonb, '4 groups of 5 is 20. Then 2 more: 20 + 2 = 22.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_easy', 1, 'Look at the array. How many rows are there?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"2"},{"id":"b","text":"3"},{"id":"c","text":"5"},{"id":"d","text":"6"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Rows go across. There are 2 rows, with 3 dots in each.', '{"kind":"array","rows":2,"columns":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_easy', 1, 'Count by fives: 5, 10, 15, ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"20"'::jsonb, 'Each jump adds 5. 15 + 5 = 20.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_easy', 1, '6 cakes shared equally between 2 plates gives 3 cakes on each plate.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, '3 + 3 = 6, so each plate gets 3.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'easy', 1, 'Look at the array. How many dots are there altogether?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"20"'::jsonb, 'There are 4 rows of 5. Count by fives: 5, 10, 15, 20.', '{"kind":"array","rows":4,"columns":5}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'easy', 1, 'Which of these shows equal groups?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"3, 3, 3"},{"id":"b","text":"2, 4, 3"},{"id":"c","text":"1, 5, 3"},{"id":"d","text":"3, 3, 2"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Equal groups all have the same number. Only 3, 3, 3 has the same number in each group.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'easy', 1, '10 children stand in 2 equal lines. How many children are in each line?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, 'Share 10 into 2 equal groups. 5 + 5 = 10, so 5 in each line.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'medium', 1, '3 × 10 = ___', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"30"'::jsonb, '3 groups of 10: 10, 20, 30.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'medium', 1, 'Which number sentences match the array? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"5 × 2"},{"id":"b","text":"2 × 5"},{"id":"c","text":"2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2"},{"id":"d","text":"5 + 2"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'There are 5 rows of 2, which is 5 × 2 or 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2. Turned around it is 2 × 5. All make 10. 5 + 2 is only 7.', '{"kind":"array","rows":5,"columns":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'medium', 1, 'A koala has 4 legs. How many legs do 4 koalas have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"16"'::jsonb, '4 groups of 4: 4, 8, 12, 16.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'hard', 1, '18 muffins are packed into boxes of 6. How many boxes are needed?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"2"},{"id":"b","text":"3"},{"id":"c","text":"4"},{"id":"d","text":"12"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'Count by sixes until you reach 18: 6, 12, 18. That is 3 boxes.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'hard', 1, '16 marbles are shared equally into 4 bags. How many marbles go in each bag?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"4"'::jsonb, '4 bags of 4 is 4 + 4 + 4 + 4 = 16, so each bag gets 4.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'hard', 1, 'An array with 3 rows of 7 has the same number of dots as an array with 7 rows of 3.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Turning an array around does not change how many dots it has. Both have 21 dots.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_hard', 1, 'Each tent sleeps 4 children. How many tents are needed for 18 children?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, '4 tents sleep 16 children. 2 children are left, so they need 1 more tent. That is 5 tents.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_hard', 1, 'Tom has 4 bags with 5 lollies in each. Mia has 3 bags with 6 lollies in each. Who has more lollies?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Tom"},{"id":"b","text":"Mia"},{"id":"c","text":"They have the same"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Tom has 5, 10, 15, 20 lollies. Mia has 6, 12, 18 lollies. 20 is more than 18.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002030130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020301', 'very_hard', 1, 'Put these in order from fewest things to most things.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"2 groups of 6"},{"id":"b","text":"3 groups of 5"},{"id":"c","text":"4 groups of 4"},{"id":"d","text":"5 groups of 5"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, '2 groups of 6 is 12, 3 groups of 5 is 15, 4 groups of 4 is 16, and 5 groups of 5 is 25.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_easy', 1, 'What fraction is shaded?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"one half"},{"id":"b","text":"one quarter"},{"id":"c","text":"one eighth"},{"id":"d","text":"two"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The circle is cut into 2 equal parts and 1 is shaded. That is one half.', '{"kind":"fraction","shape":"circle","parts":2,"shaded":1}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_easy', 1, 'When you cut something into 2 equal parts, each part is one half.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, '2 equal parts are called halves.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_easy', 1, 'What fraction of the bar is shaded?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["1/4","one quarter","a quarter","quarter","one fourth"]'::jsonb, 'The bar has 4 equal parts and 1 is shaded. That is one quarter.', '{"kind":"fraction","shape":"bar","parts":4,"shaded":1}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'easy', 1, 'How many quarters make a whole?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"2"},{"id":"b","text":"3"},{"id":"c","text":"4"},{"id":"d","text":"8"}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, 'A whole cut into quarters has 4 equal parts.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'easy', 1, 'What is half of 10?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, 'Share 10 into 2 equal groups. 5 + 5 = 10, so half is 5.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'easy', 1, 'What fraction is shaded?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"one half"},{"id":"b","text":"one quarter"},{"id":"c","text":"one eighth"},{"id":"d","text":"eight"}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, 'The circle has 8 equal parts and 1 is shaded. That is one eighth.', '{"kind":"fraction","shape":"circle","parts":8,"shaded":1}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'medium', 1, 'A ribbon is 12 cm long. Lucy cuts it in half. How long is each piece?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["6","6 cm"]'::jsonb, 'Half of 12 is 6, because 6 + 6 = 12. Each piece is 6 cm.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'medium', 1, 'What fraction of the bar is shaded?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["3/8","three eighths"]'::jsonb, 'The bar has 8 equal parts and 3 are shaded. That is three eighths.', '{"kind":"fraction","shape":"bar","parts":8,"shaded":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'medium', 1, 'Which of these make one whole? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"2 halves"},{"id":"b","text":"4 quarters"},{"id":"c","text":"8 eighths"},{"id":"d","text":"3 quarters"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, '2 halves, 4 quarters and 8 eighths each fill the whole. 3 quarters is one quarter short.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'hard', 1, 'What is one quarter of 8?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"2"'::jsonb, 'Share 8 into 4 equal groups. Each group has 2.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'hard', 1, 'Which piece of the same pizza is bigger: one half or one quarter?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"one half"},{"id":"b","text":"one quarter"},{"id":"c","text":"They are the same"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Cutting into 2 parts makes bigger pieces than cutting into 4 parts. One half is bigger.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'hard', 1, 'Two quarters of this circle are shaded. That is the same as one half.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, '2 of the 4 equal parts are shaded. That covers half the circle.', '{"kind":"fraction","shape":"circle","parts":4,"shaded":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_hard', 1, 'Put these pieces of the same cake in order from smallest to largest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"one eighth"},{"id":"b","text":"one quarter"},{"id":"c","text":"one half"},{"id":"d","text":"the whole cake"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'The more equal parts you cut, the smaller each part. Eighths are smallest, then quarters, then halves, then the whole.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_hard', 1, 'Look at the ribbon on the ruler. How long is one quarter of the ribbon?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["2","2 cm"]'::jsonb, 'The ribbon is 8 cm long. Share 8 into 4 equal parts: each part is 2 cm.', '{"kind":"ruler","cm":12,"length":8,"object":"ribbon"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_hard', 1, 'A rope is 16 metres long. Max cuts it into eighths. How long is each piece?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["2","2 m","2 metres"]'::jsonb, 'Eighths means 8 equal pieces. 8 pieces of 2 metres make 16 metres.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_easy', 1, 'Half of this bar is shaded.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The bar has 2 equal parts and 1 is shaded. That is one half.', '{"kind":"fraction","shape":"bar","parts":2,"shaded":1}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_easy', 1, 'Ava cuts an apple into 2 equal parts. What is each part called?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"a half"},{"id":"b","text":"a quarter"},{"id":"c","text":"an eighth"},{"id":"d","text":"a whole"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '2 equal parts are called halves. Each part is a half.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_easy', 1, 'How much of the circle is shaded?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"one quarter"},{"id":"b","text":"one half"},{"id":"c","text":"the whole circle"},{"id":"d","text":"none of it"}]'::jsonb, '"c"'::jsonb, 'All 4 quarters are shaded, so the whole circle is shaded.', '{"kind":"fraction","shape":"circle","parts":4,"shaded":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'easy', 1, 'What is half of 14?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"7"'::jsonb, 'Share 14 into 2 equal groups. 7 + 7 = 14, so half is 7.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'easy', 1, 'A sandwich is cut into 2 pieces that are not the same size. Each piece is a half.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'Halves must be equal. If the pieces are different sizes, they are not halves.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'easy', 1, 'What fraction is shaded?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"one quarter"},{"id":"b","text":"three quarters"},{"id":"c","text":"three eighths"},{"id":"d","text":"one half"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'The circle has 4 equal parts and 3 are shaded. That is three quarters.', '{"kind":"fraction","shape":"circle","parts":4,"shaded":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'medium', 1, 'One whole is ___ eighths.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"8"'::jsonb, 'A whole cut into eighths has 8 equal parts.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'medium', 1, 'Look at the pencil on the ruler. How long is half of the pencil?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["5","5 cm"]'::jsonb, 'The pencil is 10 cm long. Half of 10 is 5, so half the pencil is 5 cm.', '{"kind":"ruler","cm":12,"length":10,"object":"pencil"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'medium', 1, 'How many eighths make one half?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"2"},{"id":"b","text":"4"},{"id":"c","text":"6"},{"id":"d","text":"8"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, '8 eighths make a whole, so half of that is 4 eighths.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'hard', 1, 'Which of these tell how much of the bar is shaded? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"six eighths"},{"id":"b","text":"three quarters"},{"id":"c","text":"one half"},{"id":"d","text":"two eighths"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b"]'::jsonb, '6 of the 8 equal parts are shaded: six eighths. 2 eighths make a quarter, so 6 eighths is also three quarters.', '{"kind":"fraction","shape":"bar","parts":8,"shaded":6}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'hard', 1, 'What is one quarter of 20?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, 'Share 20 into 4 equal groups. 5 + 5 + 5 + 5 = 20, so each group has 5.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'hard', 1, 'There are 30 children in a class. Half of them are girls. How many girls are there?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"15"'::jsonb, 'Half of 30 is 15, because 15 + 15 = 30.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_hard', 1, 'How many more eighths must be shaded to shade the whole bar?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"3"'::jsonb, 'The whole bar is 8 eighths. 5 are shaded, and 8 − 5 = 3 more are needed.', '{"kind":"fraction","shape":"bar","parts":8,"shaded":5}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_hard', 1, 'A path is 20 metres long. It is split into quarters. Leah walks 2 quarters of the path. How far does she walk?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"5 m"},{"id":"b","text":"10 m"},{"id":"c","text":"15 m"},{"id":"d","text":"20 m"}]'::jsonb, '"b"'::jsonb, 'One quarter of 20 is 5 metres. 2 quarters is 5 + 5 = 10 metres. That is half the path.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002040130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020401', 'very_hard', 1, 'Put these in order from smallest to largest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"one quarter of 8"},{"id":"b","text":"one half of 8"},{"id":"c","text":"three quarters of 8"},{"id":"d","text":"8"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'One quarter of 8 is 2, one half is 4, three quarters is 6, and the whole is 8.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_easy', 1, 'How long is the pencil?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["6","6 cm"]'::jsonb, 'The pencil starts at 0 and ends at 6, so it is 6 cm long.', '{"kind":"ruler","cm":10,"length":6,"object":"pencil"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which unit is best for measuring the length of the classroom?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"metres"},{"id":"b","text":"centimetres"},{"id":"c","text":"kilograms"},{"id":"d","text":"litres"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A classroom is long, so metres are best. Centimetres are for small things.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_easy', 1, 'A metre is longer than a centimetre.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A metre is 100 centimetres, so it is much longer.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'easy', 1, '1 metre = ___ centimetres', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"100"'::jsonb, 'There are 100 centimetres in 1 metre.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'easy', 1, 'How long is the ribbon?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"9 cm"},{"id":"b","text":"10 cm"},{"id":"c","text":"8 cm"},{"id":"d","text":"12 cm"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The ribbon starts at 0 and ends at 9, so it is 9 cm long.', '{"kind":"ruler","cm":12,"length":9,"object":"ribbon"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'easy', 1, 'Ava measures her desk with paper clips. Then she measures it with pencils. Which gives the bigger number?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"paper clips"},{"id":"b","text":"pencils"},{"id":"c","text":"They give the same number"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Paper clips are shorter than pencils, so it takes more of them to cover the desk.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'medium', 1, 'Put these lengths in order from shortest to longest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"8 cm"},{"id":"b","text":"30 cm"},{"id":"c","text":"1 m"},{"id":"d","text":"2 m"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, '1 m is 100 cm and 2 m is 200 cm. So the order is 8 cm, 30 cm, 1 m, 2 m.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'medium', 1, 'Jack''s pencil is 14 cm long. Mia''s pencil is 9 cm long. How much longer is Jack''s pencil?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["5","5 cm"]'::jsonb, 'Find the difference: 14 − 9 = 5. Jack''s pencil is 5 cm longer.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'medium', 1, 'Which things are longer than 1 metre? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"a car"},{"id":"b","text":"a netball court"},{"id":"c","text":"an eraser"},{"id":"d","text":"a teaspoon"},{"id":"e","text":"a school bus"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","e"]'::jsonb, 'A car, a netball court and a school bus are all longer than a big step. An eraser and a teaspoon are short.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'hard', 1, 'Look at the pencil. Sam''s crayon is 5 cm shorter. How long is Sam''s crayon?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["8","8 cm"]'::jsonb, 'The pencil is 13 cm long. 13 − 5 = 8, so the crayon is 8 cm long.', '{"kind":"ruler","cm":15,"length":13,"object":"pencil"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'hard', 1, 'A skipping rope is 2 metres long. How many centimetres is that?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"200"},{"id":"b","text":"20"},{"id":"c","text":"2"},{"id":"d","text":"102"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '1 metre is 100 cm, so 2 metres is 100 + 100 = 200 cm.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'hard', 1, 'Lily measures a table and gets 8 hand spans. Her dad gets 5 hand spans. So the table is shorter for her dad.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'It is the same table. Dad''s hand span is bigger, so he needs fewer. That is why we use units that are all the same size.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_hard', 1, 'A ribbon is 1 metre long. Ella cuts off 35 cm. How many centimetres are left?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["65","65 cm"]'::jsonb, '1 metre is 100 cm. 100 − 35 = 65, so 65 cm is left.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_hard', 1, 'A wombat walks 20 m to a log. It walks 20 m back. Then it walks 15 m to its burrow. How far does it walk altogether?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["55","55 m"]'::jsonb, 'Add the three parts: 20 + 20 = 40, and 40 + 15 = 55. It walks 55 m.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_hard', 1, 'Mel puts 4 rulers end to end along a bench. Each ruler is 30 cm long. How many centimetres long is the bench?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["120","120 cm"]'::jsonb, 'Count by 30s: 30, 60, 90, 120. The bench is 120 cm long.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_easy', 1, 'How long is the pencil?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"4 cm"},{"id":"b","text":"5 cm"},{"id":"c","text":"3 cm"},{"id":"d","text":"10 cm"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The pencil starts at 0 and ends at 4, so it is 4 cm long.', '{"kind":"ruler","cm":10,"length":4,"object":"pencil"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_easy', 1, 'When we measure with paper clips, we put them end to end with no gaps.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Gaps or overlaps make the answer wrong, so the paper clips must touch end to end.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which is longer?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"1 metre"},{"id":"b","text":"30 centimetres"},{"id":"c","text":"They are the same"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '1 metre is 100 centimetres, and 100 is more than 30.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'easy', 1, 'A stick is 7 paper clips long. A rope is 12 paper clips long. How many paper clips longer is the rope?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, '12 − 7 = 5, so the rope is 5 paper clips longer.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'easy', 1, 'How many centimetres long is the ribbon?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["11","11 cm"]'::jsonb, 'The ribbon starts at 0 and ends at 11, so it is 11 cm long.', '{"kind":"ruler","cm":15,"length":11,"object":"ribbon"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'easy', 1, '100 centimetres = ___ metre', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"1"'::jsonb, '100 centimetres make 1 metre.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'medium', 1, 'Which is the best estimate for the length of a teaspoon?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"15 cm"},{"id":"b","text":"15 m"},{"id":"c","text":"1 m"},{"id":"d","text":"1 cm"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A teaspoon is a bit longer than your hand is wide, about 15 cm. 1 cm is tiny and 1 m is as long as a big step.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'medium', 1, 'Which would you measure in metres? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"a swimming pool"},{"id":"b","text":"a gum tree''s height"},{"id":"c","text":"an ant"},{"id":"d","text":"a cricket pitch"},{"id":"e","text":"a fingernail"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Big things like a pool, a gum tree and a cricket pitch are measured in metres. An ant and a fingernail are tiny, so we use centimetres.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'medium', 1, 'Put these in order from longest to shortest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"a school hall"},{"id":"b","text":"a kangaroo''s tail"},{"id":"c","text":"a crayon"},{"id":"d","text":"a grain of rice"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A hall is many metres long, a kangaroo''s tail is about 1 metre, a crayon is a few centimetres and a grain of rice is tiny.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'hard', 1, 'Zac measures a rug with pencils but leaves gaps between them. His answer will be too small.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The gaps are not counted, so he counts fewer pencils than the rug really needs. His number is too small.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'hard', 1, 'Ruby''s block tower is 46 cm tall. Ben''s tower is 29 cm tall. How much taller is Ruby''s tower?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["17","17 cm"]'::jsonb, 'Find the difference: 46 − 29 = 17. Ruby''s tower is 17 cm taller.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'hard', 1, 'Look at the pencil. How many more centimetres would make it 10 cm long?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"3 cm"},{"id":"b","text":"7 cm"},{"id":"c","text":"10 cm"},{"id":"d","text":"17 cm"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The pencil is 7 cm long. Count on from 7 to 10: that is 3 more centimetres.', '{"kind":"ruler","cm":12,"length":7,"object":"pencil"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_hard', 1, 'A python is 2 m long. A brown snake is 85 cm long. How many centimetres longer is the python?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["115","115 cm"]'::jsonb, '2 m is 200 cm. 200 − 85 = 115, so the python is 115 cm longer.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_hard', 1, 'Each of Kai''s steps is about 50 cm long. He takes 4 steps. About how far does he walk?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"2 m"},{"id":"b","text":"4 m"},{"id":"c","text":"50 cm"},{"id":"d","text":"54 cm"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '4 steps of 50 cm is 50 + 50 + 50 + 50 = 200 cm, and 200 cm is 2 m.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020501', 'very_hard', 1, '1 m and 40 cm = ___ cm', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"140"'::jsonb, '1 m is 100 cm. 100 + 40 = 140 cm.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050201', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_easy', 1, 'How many squares are shaded?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'There are 2 rows of 3 shaded squares. 3 + 3 = 6.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":4,"rows":3,"cells":[[0,0],[1,0],[2,0],[0,1],[1,1],[2,1]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050202', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_easy', 1, 'Area is how much surface a shape covers.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Area tells us how much space the top of a shape covers.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050203', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which has the bigger area?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"a beach towel"},{"id":"b","text":"a postage stamp"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A beach towel covers much more space than a tiny stamp.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050204', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'easy', 1, 'This rectangle is covered with squares. What is its area in squares?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["8","8 squares"]'::jsonb, 'There are 2 rows with 4 squares in each row. 4 + 4 = 8 squares.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[0,0],[4,0],[4,2],[0,2]],"grid":true}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050205', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'easy', 1, 'Which is best for measuring the area of a desk?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"sticky notes"},{"id":"b","text":"a piece of string"},{"id":"c","text":"a cup"},{"id":"d","text":"a ruler"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Sticky notes are all the same size and can cover the desk with no gaps.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050206', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'easy', 1, 'When we measure area, what should the units do? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"be all the same size"},{"id":"b","text":"cover the shape with no gaps"},{"id":"c","text":"overlap each other"},{"id":"d","text":"be different sizes"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b"]'::jsonb, 'Units must be the same size and cover the shape with no gaps and no overlaps.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050207', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'medium', 1, 'A rug is covered by 3 rows of tiles. There are 5 tiles in each row. How many tiles are there?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"15"},{"id":"b","text":"8"},{"id":"c","text":"35"},{"id":"d","text":"10"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Count 3 rows of 5: 5, 10, 15. There are 15 tiles.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050208', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'medium', 1, 'What is the area of the shaded shape in squares?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["7","7 squares"]'::jsonb, 'There are 4 squares along the bottom and 3 more going up the side. 4 + 3 = 7.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":5,"rows":4,"cells":[[0,0],[1,0],[2,0],[3,0],[0,1],[0,2],[0,3]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050209', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'medium', 1, 'Put these from smallest area to largest area.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"a stamp"},{"id":"b","text":"a playing card"},{"id":"c","text":"a pillow"},{"id":"d","text":"a tennis court"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A stamp is tiny, a playing card is a bit bigger, a pillow is bigger again and a tennis court is huge.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050210', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'hard', 1, 'Ollie covers a book with 12 sticky notes. Grace covers the same book with 6 cards. Why are the numbers different?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"The cards are bigger, so fewer are needed"},{"id":"b","text":"Grace''s book is smaller"},{"id":"c","text":"Ollie''s book is bigger"},{"id":"d","text":"The sticky notes are bigger"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It is the same book. Bigger units cover more each, so Grace needs fewer cards.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050211', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'hard', 1, 'Which way finds the area of this rectangle?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"3 rows of 5 = 15"},{"id":"b","text":"3 + 5 = 8"},{"id":"c","text":"5 rows of 5 = 25"},{"id":"d","text":"3 rows of 3 = 9"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'There are 3 rows with 5 squares in each row. 5, 10, 15. The area is 15 squares.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[0,0],[5,0],[5,3],[0,3]],"grid":true}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050212', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'hard', 1, 'A shape with 2 rows of 6 squares has the same area as a shape with 3 rows of 4 squares.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, '2 rows of 6 is 12 squares. 3 rows of 4 is also 12 squares. So the areas are the same.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050213', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_hard', 1, 'A garden path has 4 rows of pavers with 5 in each row. Dad takes away 1 row. How many pavers are left?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"15"'::jsonb, 'After taking 1 row away, 3 rows are left. 3 rows of 5 is 5, 10, 15.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050214', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_hard', 1, 'Mia wants to shade the whole grid. How many more squares does she need to shade?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"15"'::jsonb, 'The grid has 4 rows of 6, which is 24 squares. 9 are shaded. 24 − 9 = 15 more.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":4,"cells":[[0,0],[1,0],[2,0],[0,1],[1,1],[2,1],[0,2],[1,2],[2,2]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050215', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which shapes have an area of 12 squares? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"3 rows of 4 squares"},{"id":"b","text":"2 rows of 6 squares"},{"id":"c","text":"5 rows of 2 squares"},{"id":"d","text":"4 rows of 4 squares"},{"id":"e","text":"6 rows of 2 squares"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","e"]'::jsonb, '3 rows of 4, 2 rows of 6 and 6 rows of 2 all make 12. 5 rows of 2 is 10 and 4 rows of 4 is 16.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050216', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_easy', 1, 'Count the squares. What is the area of this shape?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["9","9 squares"]'::jsonb, 'There are 3 rows of 3 squares. 3, 6, 9.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[0,0],[3,0],[3,3],[0,3]],"grid":true}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050217', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which covers the biggest area?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"a netball court"},{"id":"b","text":"a beach towel"},{"id":"c","text":"a book cover"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A netball court covers far more ground than a towel or a book.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050218', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_easy', 1, 'When we measure area, it is fine to leave gaps between the units.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'Gaps are not counted, so the answer would be too small. Units must cover the shape with no gaps.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050219', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'easy', 1, 'How many squares are shaded?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"5"},{"id":"b","text":"4"},{"id":"c","text":"6"},{"id":"d","text":"15"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'There are 4 shaded squares in the row and 1 on top. 4 + 1 = 5.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":5,"rows":3,"cells":[[0,1],[1,1],[2,1],[3,1],[1,2]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050220', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'easy', 1, '2 rows of 5 squares make ___ squares.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"10"'::jsonb, '5 + 5 = 10, so 2 rows of 5 make 10 squares.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050221', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'easy', 1, 'Jy''s rug is covered by 9 tiles. Ana''s rug is covered by 14 of the same tiles. Whose rug has the bigger area?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Ana''s"},{"id":"b","text":"Jy''s"},{"id":"c","text":"They are the same"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The tiles are the same size, and Ana''s rug needs more of them. So Ana''s rug is bigger.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050222', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'medium', 1, 'What is the area of this rectangle in squares?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["12","12 squares"]'::jsonb, 'There are 2 rows with 6 squares in each row. 6 + 6 = 12.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[0,0],[6,0],[6,2],[0,2]],"grid":true}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050223', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'medium', 1, 'Put these in order from smallest area to largest area.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"a coin"},{"id":"b","text":"an envelope"},{"id":"c","text":"a door"},{"id":"d","text":"a basketball court"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A coin is tiny, then an envelope, then a door, and a basketball court is the biggest.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050224', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'medium', 1, 'Which are good units for measuring the area of a table? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"sticky notes"},{"id":"b","text":"playing cards"},{"id":"c","text":"pencils"},{"id":"d","text":"exercise books"},{"id":"e","text":"string"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Sticky notes, playing cards and exercise books are flat and cover the table. Pencils and string measure length, not area.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050225', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'hard', 1, 'A tile pattern has 4 rows. Each row has 6 tiles. How many tiles are there altogether?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"24"'::jsonb, 'Count 4 rows of 6: 6, 12, 18, 24.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050226', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'hard', 1, 'Two shapes are shaded. How many more squares does the right shape have than the left shape?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"2"'::jsonb, 'The left shape has 4 squares. The right shape has 3 rows of 2, which is 6. 6 − 4 = 2.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":7,"rows":4,"cells":[[0,0],[1,0],[0,1],[1,1],[4,0],[5,0],[4,1],[5,1],[4,2],[5,2]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050227', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'hard', 1, 'Two shapes can look different but still have the same area.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A row of 4 squares and a 2 by 2 square look different, but both cover 4 squares.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050228', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_hard', 1, 'Jo covers a poster with 8 big cards. Each big card is the same as 2 small cards. How many small cards would cover the poster?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"16"},{"id":"b","text":"10"},{"id":"c","text":"4"},{"id":"d","text":"6"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Each big card needs 2 small cards. 8 lots of 2 is 16.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050229', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_hard', 1, 'What is the area of this shape in squares?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["12","12 squares"]'::jsonb, 'The bottom part is 2 rows of 4, which is 8. The top part is 2 rows of 2, which is 4. 8 + 4 = 12.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[0,0],[4,0],[4,2],[2,2],[2,4],[0,4]],"grid":true}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050230', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020502', 'very_hard', 1, 'Leo has 18 tiles. He makes a rectangle with 3 rows that are all the same. How many tiles are in each row?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'Share 18 into 3 equal rows: 6 + 6 + 6 = 18. Each row has 6 tiles.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050301', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which holds more water?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"a bucket"},{"id":"b","text":"a teacup"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A bucket is much bigger inside than a teacup, so it holds more.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050302', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_easy', 1, 'Capacity is how much a container can hold.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Capacity tells us how much fits inside a container.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050303', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_easy', 1, 'How many cubes make this model?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"4"'::jsonb, 'Count the cubes in the row: 1, 2, 3, 4.', '{"kind":"cubes","length":4,"width":1,"height":1}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050304', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'easy', 1, 'Look at the graph. Which container holds the most?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the bowl"},{"id":"b","text":"the vase"},{"id":"c","text":"the bottle"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The bowl has the tallest column. It takes 7 cups, more than the others.', '{"kind":"column_graph","title":"Cups of water to fill each container","columns":[{"label":"Vase","value":5},{"label":"Bottle","value":3},{"label":"Bowl","value":7}],"step":1}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050305', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'easy', 1, 'A jug holds 6 cups. 2 jugs hold ___ cups.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"12"'::jsonb, '6 + 6 = 12, so 2 jugs hold 12 cups.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050306', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'easy', 1, 'Put these in order from holds the least to holds the most.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"a teaspoon"},{"id":"b","text":"a mug"},{"id":"c","text":"a bucket"},{"id":"d","text":"a bath"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A teaspoon holds a tiny bit, a mug holds more, a bucket more again, and a bath holds the most.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050307', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'medium', 1, 'Look at the graph. How many more cups does the bowl hold than the bottle?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["4","4 cups"]'::jsonb, 'The bowl holds 7 cups and the bottle holds 3. 7 − 3 = 4.', '{"kind":"column_graph","title":"Cups of water to fill each container","columns":[{"label":"Vase","value":5},{"label":"Bottle","value":3},{"label":"Bowl","value":7}],"step":1}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050308', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'medium', 1, 'We compare containers by filling them with cups of water. What should we do? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"use the same size cup each time"},{"id":"b","text":"fill each cup to the top"},{"id":"c","text":"use a different cup for each container"},{"id":"d","text":"spill some water"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b"]'::jsonb, 'To be fair, use the same cup every time and fill it to the top each time.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050309', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'medium', 1, 'How many cubes are in this model?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'There are 2 rows of 3 cubes. 3 + 3 = 6.', '{"kind":"cubes","length":3,"width":2,"height":1}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050310', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'hard', 1, 'Ned fills a bottle with 8 small cups. Kim fills the same bottle with 4 big cups. So the bottle holds more for Ned.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'It is the same bottle, so it holds the same amount. Ned''s cups are smaller, so he needs more of them.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050311', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'hard', 1, 'A bucket holds 10 cups of water. Amir has poured in 4 cups. How many more cups will fill it?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"6"},{"id":"b","text":"14"},{"id":"c","text":"4"},{"id":"d","text":"10"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Count on from 4 to 10: that is 6 more cups. Or 10 − 4 = 6.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050312', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'hard', 1, 'How many cubes are in this model?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"8"},{"id":"b","text":"4"},{"id":"c","text":"6"},{"id":"d","text":"12"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'There are 2 layers. Each layer has 2 rows of 2, which is 4. 4 + 4 = 8. Some cubes are hidden at the back.', '{"kind":"cubes","length":2,"width":2,"height":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050313', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_hard', 1, 'A water bottle holds 3 cups. How many cups do 5 bottles hold?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["15","15 cups"]'::jsonb, 'Count by 3s five times: 3, 6, 9, 12, 15.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050314', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_hard', 1, 'Look at the table. How many scoops do the pot and the bucket hold together?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"19"},{"id":"b","text":"22"},{"id":"c","text":"27"},{"id":"d","text":"5"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The bucket holds 12 and the pot holds 7. 12 + 7 = 19.', '{"kind":"table","headings":["Container","Scoops of sand"],"rows":[["Bucket",12],["Pot",7],["Tub",15]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050315', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_hard', 1, 'Container A holds 9 cups. Container B holds 3 cups less than A. Container C holds 2 cups more than B. Which holds the most?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Container A"},{"id":"b","text":"Container B"},{"id":"c","text":"Container C"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'B holds 9 − 3 = 6 cups. C holds 6 + 2 = 8 cups. A holds 9, which is the most.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050316', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_easy', 1, 'How many cubes long is this model?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"5"},{"id":"b","text":"4"},{"id":"c","text":"6"},{"id":"d","text":"1"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Count the cubes along the row: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5.', '{"kind":"cubes","length":5,"width":1,"height":1}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050317', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which holds the least?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"an egg cup"},{"id":"b","text":"a saucepan"},{"id":"c","text":"a wheelie bin"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'An egg cup is very small inside, so it holds the least.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050318', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_easy', 1, 'A full bath holds more water than a full glass.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A bath is much bigger inside than a glass.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050319', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'easy', 1, 'Look at the graph. How many cups does the blue bottle hold?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["6","6 cups"]'::jsonb, 'Count the stars for the blue bottle: 6.', '{"kind":"picture_graph","title":"Cups to fill each bottle","thing":"cups","each":1,"rows":[{"label":"Red bottle","count":4},{"label":"Blue bottle","count":6},{"label":"Green bottle","count":3}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050320', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'easy', 1, 'Look at the graph. Which bottle holds the least?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the green bottle"},{"id":"b","text":"the red bottle"},{"id":"c","text":"the blue bottle"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The green bottle has the fewest stars, only 3 cups.', '{"kind":"picture_graph","title":"Cups to fill each bottle","thing":"cups","each":1,"rows":[{"label":"Red bottle","count":4},{"label":"Blue bottle","count":6},{"label":"Green bottle","count":3}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050321', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'easy', 1, 'A pot holds 9 cups. It has 5 cups in it. It needs ___ more cups to be full.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"4"'::jsonb, 'Count on from 5 to 9: 6, 7, 8, 9. That is 4 more cups.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050322', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'medium', 1, 'How many cubes are in this model?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"8"'::jsonb, 'There are 2 rows of 4 cubes. 4 + 4 = 8.', '{"kind":"cubes","length":4,"width":2,"height":1}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050323', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'medium', 1, 'Put these in order from holds the most to holds the least.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"a swimming pool"},{"id":"b","text":"a bath"},{"id":"c","text":"a bucket"},{"id":"d","text":"a cup"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A pool holds the most, then a bath, then a bucket, and a cup holds the least.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050324', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'medium', 1, 'Which are good units for measuring how much a container holds? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"cups"},{"id":"b","text":"spoons"},{"id":"c","text":"scoops"},{"id":"d","text":"rulers"},{"id":"e","text":"paper clips"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'Cups, spoons and scoops can be filled and poured. Rulers and paper clips measure length.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050325', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'hard', 1, 'A full rainwater tank holds 20 buckets of water. 7 buckets are used on the garden. How many buckets are left?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["13","13 buckets"]'::jsonb, '20 − 7 = 13. There are 13 buckets of water left.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050326', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'hard', 1, 'How many cubes are in this model?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"12"},{"id":"b","text":"7"},{"id":"c","text":"10"},{"id":"d","text":"6"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Each layer has 2 rows of 3, which is 6. There are 2 layers. 6 + 6 = 12.', '{"kind":"cubes","length":3,"width":2,"height":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050327', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'hard', 1, 'Using the same cup, a jar holds 5 cups and a vase holds 5 cups. So they hold the same amount.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Both were filled with the same cup and both took 5, so they hold the same amount.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050328', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_hard', 1, 'One jug fills 3 glasses. How many jugs are needed to fill 12 glasses?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"4"},{"id":"b","text":"3"},{"id":"c","text":"9"},{"id":"d","text":"36"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Count by 3s until you reach 12: 3, 6, 9, 12. That is 4 jugs.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050329', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_hard', 1, 'Look at the graph. How many scoops do all three jars hold together?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["26","26 scoops"]'::jsonb, 'Jar A holds 8, Jar B holds 12 and Jar C holds 6. 8 + 12 = 20, and 20 + 6 = 26.', '{"kind":"column_graph","title":"Scoops of rice to fill each jar","columns":[{"label":"Jar A","value":8},{"label":"Jar B","value":12},{"label":"Jar C","value":6}],"step":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050330', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020503', 'very_hard', 1, 'Ivy builds a model with 3 layers of cubes. Each layer has 4 cubes. She takes off the top layer. How many cubes are left?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"8"'::jsonb, 'Taking off 1 layer leaves 2 layers. 2 layers of 4 is 4 + 4 = 8.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050401', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_easy', 1, 'A balance scale tips down on one side. Which side is heavier?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the side that goes down"},{"id":"b","text":"the side that goes up"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The heavier side pushes down, so the side that goes down is heavier.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050402', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_easy', 1, 'A brick is heavier than a feather.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A brick is very heavy and a feather is very light.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050403', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which is the lightest?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"a leaf"},{"id":"b","text":"a watermelon"},{"id":"c","text":"a school bag"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A leaf is so light it can blow away.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050404', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'easy', 1, 'A teddy balances 9 blocks. A ball balances 6 of the same blocks. How many more blocks does the teddy balance?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"3"'::jsonb, '9 − 6 = 3. The teddy balances 3 more blocks.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050405', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'easy', 1, 'Look at the table. Which fruit is the heaviest?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the orange"},{"id":"b","text":"the apple"},{"id":"c","text":"the lemon"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The orange needs the most marbles to balance it, 15, so it is the heaviest.', '{"kind":"table","headings":["Fruit","Marbles to balance"],"rows":[["Apple",12],["Orange",15],["Lemon",9]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050406', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'easy', 1, 'When both sides of a balance scale are level, the two things have the ___ mass.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '["same","equal"]'::jsonb, 'Level means neither side is heavier, so the masses are the same.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050407', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'medium', 1, 'Look at the table. Put the fruit in order from lightest to heaviest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"lemon"},{"id":"b","text":"apple"},{"id":"c","text":"orange"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'The lemon needs 9 marbles, the apple 12 and the orange 15. Fewer marbles means lighter.', '{"kind":"table","headings":["Fruit","Marbles to balance"],"rows":[["Apple",12],["Orange",15],["Lemon",9]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050408', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'medium', 1, 'Which are good units to use on a balance scale? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"marbles that are all the same"},{"id":"b","text":"blocks that are all the same"},{"id":"c","text":"a mix of rocks"},{"id":"d","text":"pegs that are all the same"},{"id":"e","text":"toys of all sizes"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Units must all be the same mass. Same marbles, same blocks and same pegs work. Mixed rocks and toys do not.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050409', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'medium', 1, 'A big object is always heavier than a small object.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'Not always. A big balloon is lighter than a small rock.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050410', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'hard', 1, 'A pencil case balances 14 cubes. A lunchbox balances 20 cubes. How many more cubes does the lunchbox balance?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, '20 − 14 = 6. The lunchbox balances 6 more cubes.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050411', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'hard', 1, 'Look at the graph. Which two toys together balance the truck?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the car and the ball"},{"id":"b","text":"the doll and the ball"},{"id":"c","text":"the car and the doll"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The truck balances 14 pegs. The car is 8 and the ball is 6, and 8 + 6 = 14.', '{"kind":"column_graph","title":"Pegs to balance each toy","columns":[{"label":"Car","value":8},{"label":"Doll","value":12},{"label":"Ball","value":6},{"label":"Truck","value":14}],"step":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050412', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'hard', 1, 'Ella balances a book with 30 marbles. Sam balances the same book with 10 blocks. Which is heavier?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"one block"},{"id":"b","text":"one marble"},{"id":"c","text":"They are the same"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Sam needed fewer blocks than Ella needed marbles, so each block must be heavier than each marble.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050413', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_hard', 1, 'One apple balances 3 plums. How many plums balance 4 apples?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["12","12 plums"]'::jsonb, 'Each apple needs 3 plums. Count by 3s four times: 3, 6, 9, 12.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050414', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_hard', 1, 'A box balances 10 blocks. Then 2 blocks are taken off. Now the box side goes down.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The box is the same as 10 blocks. Only 8 blocks are left on the other side, so the box is heavier and goes down.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050415', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_hard', 1, 'The kangaroo toy is heavier than the koala toy. The koala toy is heavier than the possum toy. Which toy is the lightest?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the possum toy"},{"id":"b","text":"the koala toy"},{"id":"c","text":"the kangaroo toy"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The kangaroo is heavier than the koala, and the koala is heavier than the possum. So the possum is the lightest.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050416', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_easy', 1, 'On a balance scale, the lighter side goes up.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The heavier side goes down, so the lighter side goes up.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050417', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which is heavier?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"a bag of potatoes"},{"id":"b","text":"a balloon"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A bag of potatoes is heavy. A balloon is very light.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050418', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_easy', 1, 'Look at the graph. How many blocks balance Dino?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["4","4 blocks"]'::jsonb, 'Count the stars next to Dino: 4.', '{"kind":"picture_graph","title":"Blocks to balance each toy","thing":"blocks","each":1,"rows":[{"label":"Ted","count":7},{"label":"Dino","count":4},{"label":"Bunny","count":9}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050419', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'easy', 1, 'Look at the graph. Which toy is the heaviest?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Bunny"},{"id":"b","text":"Ted"},{"id":"c","text":"Dino"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Bunny needs the most blocks, 9, so Bunny is heaviest.', '{"kind":"picture_graph","title":"Blocks to balance each toy","thing":"blocks","each":1,"rows":[{"label":"Ted","count":7},{"label":"Dino","count":4},{"label":"Bunny","count":9}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050420', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'easy', 1, 'A cup balances 8 pegs. A spoon balances 3 pegs. The cup is ___ pegs heavier.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, '8 − 3 = 5, so the cup is 5 pegs heavier.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050421', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'easy', 1, 'Put these in order from lightest to heaviest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"a feather"},{"id":"b","text":"an apple"},{"id":"c","text":"a pumpkin"},{"id":"d","text":"a car"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A feather is the lightest, then an apple, then a pumpkin, and a car is the heaviest.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050422', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'medium', 1, 'Which things are heavier than a school book? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"a bike"},{"id":"b","text":"a big watermelon"},{"id":"c","text":"a paper clip"},{"id":"d","text":"a sheet of paper"},{"id":"e","text":"a fridge"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","e"]'::jsonb, 'A bike, a big watermelon and a fridge are all heavier than a book. A paper clip and a sheet of paper are lighter.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050423', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'medium', 1, 'A shoe balances 15 cubes. A hat balances 7 cubes. How many cubes balance the shoe and the hat together?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["22","22 cubes"]'::jsonb, '15 + 7 = 22 cubes.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050424', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'medium', 1, 'Why should we use marbles that are all the same to weigh things?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"So we can compare the results fairly"},{"id":"b","text":"So the scale looks nice"},{"id":"c","text":"Because marbles are heavy"},{"id":"d","text":"So the answer is always 10"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'If every marble has the same mass, we can fairly compare how many each thing needs.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050425', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'hard', 1, 'Look at the table. How many more pegs does the rock need than the shell?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["8","8 pegs"]'::jsonb, 'The rock needs 21 and the shell needs 13. 21 − 13 = 8.', '{"kind":"table","headings":["Object","Pegs to balance"],"rows":[["Shell",13],["Rock",21],["Pine cone",8]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050426', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'hard', 1, 'A pillow is bigger than a tin of beans, so the pillow must be heavier.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'A pillow is big but soft and light. The small tin of beans is heavier. Size does not tell us mass.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050427', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'hard', 1, 'Two pears balance 1 mango. The mango balances 10 cubes. How many cubes balance 1 pear?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"5"},{"id":"b","text":"10"},{"id":"c","text":"20"},{"id":"d","text":"2"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Two pears together are 10 cubes. Share 10 into 2 equal parts: 5 cubes for each pear.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050428', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_hard', 1, 'A melon balances 4 oranges. Each orange balances 5 blocks. How many blocks balance the melon?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["20","20 blocks"]'::jsonb, '4 oranges of 5 blocks each: 5, 10, 15, 20. The melon balances 20 blocks.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050429', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_hard', 1, 'Box A is heavier than Box B. Box C is heavier than Box A. Put the boxes in order from heaviest to lightest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"Box C"},{"id":"b","text":"Box A"},{"id":"c","text":"Box B"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'C is heavier than A, and A is heavier than B. So the order is C, A, B.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002050430', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020504', 'very_hard', 1, 'Look at the table. What would balance the robot?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the train and the kite"},{"id":"b","text":"two kites"},{"id":"c","text":"two trains"},{"id":"d","text":"the kite and 7 blocks"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The train and kite together are 11 + 7 = 18 blocks, the same as the robot. Two kites are 14 and two trains are 22.', '{"kind":"table","headings":["Toy","Blocks to balance"],"rows":[["Robot",18],["Train",11],["Kite",7]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_easy', 1, 'What time does the clock show?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"half past 3"},{"id":"b","text":"3 o''clock"},{"id":"c","text":"half past 6"},{"id":"d","text":"quarter past 3"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The long hand points to 6, so it is half past. The short hand is between 3 and 4, so it is half past 3.', '{"kind":"clock","hour":3,"minute":30}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_easy', 1, 'How many days are in a week?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"7"'::jsonb, 'Monday to Sunday is 7 days.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_easy', 1, 'There are 12 months in a year.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'January to December is 12 months.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'easy', 1, 'What time does the clock show?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"quarter past 9"},{"id":"b","text":"quarter to 9"},{"id":"c","text":"half past 9"},{"id":"d","text":"9 o''clock"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The long hand points to 3, a quarter of the way round. The short hand is just past 9. So it is quarter past 9.', '{"kind":"clock","hour":9,"minute":15}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'easy', 1, 'Put these months in order.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"May"},{"id":"b","text":"June"},{"id":"c","text":"July"},{"id":"d","text":"August"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'In the calendar, May comes first, then June, July and August.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'easy', 1, '1 hour = ___ minutes', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"60"'::jsonb, 'There are 60 minutes in 1 hour.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'medium', 1, 'What time does the clock show?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"quarter to 5"},{"id":"b","text":"quarter to 4"},{"id":"c","text":"quarter past 4"},{"id":"d","text":"quarter past 9"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The long hand points to 9, so it is quarter to. The short hand is nearly at 5, so it is quarter to 5.', '{"kind":"clock","hour":4,"minute":45}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'medium', 1, 'Write quarter past 7 as a digital time.', 'short_answer', NULL, '["7:15"]'::jsonb, 'Quarter past is 15 minutes past, so it is 7:15.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'medium', 1, 'School starts at 9 o''clock and finishes at 3 o''clock. How many hours long is the school day?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"6"},{"id":"b","text":"3"},{"id":"c","text":"12"},{"id":"d","text":"9"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Count the hours from 9: 10, 11, 12, 1, 2, 3. That is 6 hours.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'hard', 1, 'Which months have 31 days? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"January"},{"id":"b","text":"February"},{"id":"c","text":"March"},{"id":"d","text":"April"},{"id":"e","text":"December"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c","e"]'::jsonb, 'January, March and December have 31 days. April has 30 days and February has 28 or 29.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'hard', 1, 'What time will it be in half an hour?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"half past 2"},{"id":"b","text":"half past 3"},{"id":"c","text":"quarter past 2"},{"id":"d","text":"3 o''clock"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The clock shows 2 o''clock. Half an hour later the long hand is on 6, so it is half past 2.', '{"kind":"clock","hour":2,"minute":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'hard', 1, 'Quarter to 6 is the same as 5:45.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Quarter to 6 is 15 minutes before 6, which is 5:45.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_hard', 1, 'Today is Monday. What day will it be in 9 days?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["Wednesday","Wed"]'::jsonb, 'In 7 days it is Monday again. 2 more days is Tuesday, then Wednesday.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_hard', 1, 'Netball starts at the time on the clock. The game goes for 30 minutes. What time does it finish?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"quarter past 11"},{"id":"b","text":"quarter to 11"},{"id":"c","text":"11 o''clock"},{"id":"d","text":"half past 11"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The clock shows quarter to 11. 15 minutes later is 11 o''clock, and 15 more minutes is quarter past 11.', '{"kind":"clock","hour":10,"minute":45}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_hard', 1, 'It is 7 June. The school holidays start on 21 June. How many weeks away are the holidays?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["2","2 weeks"]'::jsonb, 'From 7 June to 21 June is 14 days. 7 days is a week, so 14 days is 2 weeks.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_easy', 1, 'What time does the clock show?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["6 o''clock","6:00","6","six o''clock"]'::jsonb, 'The long hand points to 12 and the short hand points to 6. It is 6 o''clock.', '{"kind":"clock","hour":6,"minute":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which day comes after Friday?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Saturday"},{"id":"b","text":"Thursday"},{"id":"c","text":"Sunday"},{"id":"d","text":"Monday"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The days go Thursday, Friday, Saturday.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_easy', 1, 'Half past 8 is the same as 8:30.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Half past means 30 minutes past, so half past 8 is 8:30.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'easy', 1, 'What time does the clock show?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"quarter past 11"},{"id":"b","text":"quarter to 11"},{"id":"c","text":"quarter past 3"},{"id":"d","text":"half past 11"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The long hand points to 3, so it is quarter past. The short hand is just past 11. So it is quarter past 11.', '{"kind":"clock","hour":11,"minute":15}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'easy', 1, '2 weeks = ___ days', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"14"'::jsonb, '1 week is 7 days, so 2 weeks is 7 + 7 = 14 days.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'easy', 1, 'Put these in order from shortest time to longest time.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"1 minute"},{"id":"b","text":"1 hour"},{"id":"c","text":"1 day"},{"id":"d","text":"1 week"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A minute is short, an hour is 60 minutes, a day is 24 hours and a week is 7 days.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'medium', 1, 'What time does the clock show?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"quarter to 2"},{"id":"b","text":"quarter to 1"},{"id":"c","text":"quarter past 1"},{"id":"d","text":"half past 1"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The long hand points to 9, so it is quarter to. The short hand is nearly at 2. So it is quarter to 2.', '{"kind":"clock","hour":1,"minute":45}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'medium', 1, 'Which season comes after winter?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"spring"},{"id":"b","text":"summer"},{"id":"c","text":"autumn"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The seasons go summer, autumn, winter, spring.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'medium', 1, 'Write half past 4 as a digital time.', 'short_answer', NULL, '["4:30"]'::jsonb, 'Half past is 30 minutes past, so it is 4:30.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'hard', 1, 'Which are the same time as quarter to 9? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"8:45"},{"id":"b","text":"9:45"},{"id":"c","text":"15 minutes before 9 o''clock"},{"id":"d","text":"9:15"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c"]'::jsonb, 'Quarter to 9 is 15 minutes before 9 o''clock. That is 8:45.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'hard', 1, 'Dinner is in a quarter of an hour. What time will dinner be?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"quarter to 6"},{"id":"b","text":"quarter past 5"},{"id":"c","text":"quarter to 5"},{"id":"d","text":"6 o''clock"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The clock shows half past 5. A quarter of an hour is 15 minutes. 5:30 + 15 minutes is 5:45, which is quarter to 6.', '{"kind":"clock","hour":5,"minute":30}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'hard', 1, 'A movie goes from 3 o''clock to half past 4. It is 1 and a half hours long.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'From 3 o''clock to 4 o''clock is 1 hour. From 4 o''clock to half past 4 is half an hour. So it is 1 and a half hours.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_hard', 1, 'A sausage sizzle starts at quarter past 11. It goes for 2 hours. What time does it finish?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["1:15","quarter past 1","1:15 pm","1:15pm"]'::jsonb, 'Count on 2 hours from quarter past 11: quarter past 12, then quarter past 1.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_hard', 1, 'Ruby''s birthday is 3 weeks after 2 March. What date is her birthday?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"23 March"},{"id":"b","text":"5 March"},{"id":"c","text":"9 March"},{"id":"d","text":"16 March"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '3 weeks is 21 days. Count on a week at a time: 9 March, 16 March, 23 March.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002060130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020601', 'very_hard', 1, 'The clock shows when Tom started reading. He read until 9:30. How many minutes did he read?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["45","45 minutes"]'::jsonb, 'The clock shows 8:45. From 8:45 to 9:00 is 15 minutes. From 9:00 to 9:30 is 30 minutes. 15 + 30 = 45.', '{"kind":"clock","hour":8,"minute":45}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_easy', 1, 'What is the name of this shape?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"pentagon"},{"id":"b","text":"hexagon"},{"id":"c","text":"triangle"},{"id":"d","text":"octagon"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Count the sides: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. A shape with 5 sides is a pentagon.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[3,0],[7,0],[9,4],[5,7],[1,4]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_easy', 1, 'How many sides does a square have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"4"'::jsonb, 'A square has 4 straight sides that are all the same length.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_easy', 1, 'A circle has no corners.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A circle has one curved edge and no corners at all.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'easy', 1, 'How many sides does this shape have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'Count each straight side: there are 6. It is a hexagon.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[2,0],[6,0],[8,3],[6,6],[2,6],[0,3]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'easy', 1, 'What do we call any shape with 4 straight sides?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"quadrilateral"},{"id":"b","text":"pentagon"},{"id":"c","text":"triangle"},{"id":"d","text":"hexagon"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Quad means 4. Any shape with 4 straight sides is a quadrilateral.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'easy', 1, 'Which shapes are quadrilaterals? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"square"},{"id":"b","text":"rectangle"},{"id":"c","text":"triangle"},{"id":"d","text":"rhombus"},{"id":"e","text":"pentagon"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'A square, a rectangle and a rhombus each have 4 sides. A triangle has 3 and a pentagon has 5.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'medium', 1, 'What is this shape called?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"octagon"},{"id":"b","text":"hexagon"},{"id":"c","text":"pentagon"},{"id":"d","text":"rectangle"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It has 8 sides. A shape with 8 sides is an octagon, like a stop sign.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[3,0],[6,0],[8,2],[8,5],[6,7],[3,7],[1,5],[1,2]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'medium', 1, 'Put these shapes in order from fewest sides to most sides.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"triangle"},{"id":"b","text":"square"},{"id":"c","text":"pentagon"},{"id":"d","text":"hexagon"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A triangle has 3 sides, a square 4, a pentagon 5 and a hexagon 6.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'medium', 1, 'This shape is a quadrilateral.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'It has 4 straight sides, so it is a quadrilateral. It is a rhombus.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[4,0],[7,4],[4,8],[1,4]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'hard', 1, 'How many corners do 2 triangles have altogether?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'Each triangle has 3 corners. 3 + 3 = 6.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'hard', 1, 'This shape has 4 sides, but it is not a rectangle. Why not?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Its corners are not square corners"},{"id":"b","text":"It has 5 sides"},{"id":"c","text":"It has curved sides"},{"id":"d","text":"It has no corners"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A rectangle has 4 square corners. This shape is leaning over, so its corners are not square.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[0,0],[6,0],[8,4],[2,4]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'hard', 1, 'Which shapes have more than 4 corners? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"hexagon"},{"id":"b","text":"pentagon"},{"id":"c","text":"square"},{"id":"d","text":"triangle"},{"id":"e","text":"octagon"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","e"]'::jsonb, 'A hexagon has 6 corners, a pentagon 5 and an octagon 8. A square has 4 and a triangle 3.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_hard', 1, 'Jai draws a pentagon and a hexagon. How many sides has he drawn altogether?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"11"'::jsonb, 'A pentagon has 5 sides and a hexagon has 6. 5 + 6 = 11.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_hard', 1, 'This square is cut in half with a straight line from one corner to the opposite corner. What two shapes do you get?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"2 triangles"},{"id":"b","text":"2 squares"},{"id":"c","text":"2 rectangles"},{"id":"d","text":"2 circles"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The line goes from corner to corner, so each half has 3 sides and 3 corners. They are 2 triangles.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[2,1],[8,1],[8,7],[2,7]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_hard', 1, 'I have 4 straight sides that are all the same length. My corners are not square corners. What am I?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"rhombus"},{"id":"b","text":"square"},{"id":"c","text":"rectangle"},{"id":"d","text":"trapezium"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A square also has 4 equal sides, but its corners are square. A shape with 4 equal sides and no square corners is a rhombus.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_easy', 1, 'What shape is this?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"square"},{"id":"b","text":"triangle"},{"id":"c","text":"pentagon"},{"id":"d","text":"circle"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It has 4 sides that are all the same length and 4 square corners. It is a square.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[2,1],[7,1],[7,6],[2,6]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_easy', 1, 'A triangle has 3 sides.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Tri means 3. A triangle has 3 sides and 3 corners.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_easy', 1, 'How many corners does a rectangle have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"4"'::jsonb, 'A rectangle has 4 square corners.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'easy', 1, 'How many sides does this shape have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"4"'::jsonb, 'Count the straight sides: 1, 2, 3, 4. It is a trapezium.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[0,0],[8,0],[6,4],[2,4]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'easy', 1, 'A shape has 8 sides. What is it called?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"octagon"},{"id":"b","text":"hexagon"},{"id":"c","text":"pentagon"},{"id":"d","text":"rectangle"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Octo means 8, like an octopus with 8 arms.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'easy', 1, 'Which words describe this shape? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"has 3 sides"},{"id":"b","text":"has 3 corners"},{"id":"c","text":"is a quadrilateral"},{"id":"d","text":"has curved sides"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b"]'::jsonb, 'It is a triangle. It has 3 straight sides and 3 corners. A quadrilateral has 4 sides.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[1,1],[8,1],[4,7]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'medium', 1, 'What is this shape called?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"kite"},{"id":"b","text":"rhombus"},{"id":"c","text":"triangle"},{"id":"d","text":"hexagon"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It has 4 sides. The two short sides at the top match, and the two long sides at the bottom match. It is a kite.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[4,0],[6,5],[4,7],[2,5]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070123', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'medium', 1, 'Put these shapes in order from most corners to fewest corners.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"octagon"},{"id":"b","text":"hexagon"},{"id":"c","text":"pentagon"},{"id":"d","text":"square"},{"id":"e","text":"triangle"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d","e"]'::jsonb, 'An octagon has 8 corners, a hexagon 6, a pentagon 5, a square 4 and a triangle 3.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070124', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'medium', 1, 'A pentagon has ___ corners.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, 'A pentagon has 5 sides and 5 corners.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070125', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'hard', 1, 'What is this shape called?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"hexagon"},{"id":"b","text":"octagon"},{"id":"c","text":"rectangle"},{"id":"d","text":"pentagon"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Count the sides carefully: there are 6. Any shape with 6 straight sides is a hexagon, even if it looks like an L.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[0,0],[6,0],[6,3],[3,3],[3,6],[0,6]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070126', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'hard', 1, 'Which shapes have only straight sides? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"triangle"},{"id":"b","text":"circle"},{"id":"c","text":"hexagon"},{"id":"d","text":"oval"},{"id":"e","text":"rectangle"}]'::jsonb, '["a","c","e"]'::jsonb, 'Triangles, hexagons and rectangles have straight sides. Circles and ovals are curved.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070127', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'hard', 1, 'A shape with 5 straight sides always has 5 corners.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'Each corner is where two sides meet. A closed shape with 5 sides has 5 corners.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070128', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_hard', 1, 'How many sides do 3 squares have altogether?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"12"'::jsonb, 'Each square has 4 sides. 4 + 4 + 4 = 12.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070129', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_hard', 1, 'Ari puts 2 same-sized squares side by side with no gap. What shape does he make?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"rectangle"},{"id":"b","text":"triangle"},{"id":"c","text":"hexagon"},{"id":"d","text":"circle"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Together they make a long shape with 4 square corners and 4 sides. It is a rectangle.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070130', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020701', 'very_hard', 1, 'Mia says this house shape is a hexagon. Is she right?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"No, it has 5 sides, so it is a pentagon"},{"id":"b","text":"Yes, it has 6 sides"},{"id":"c","text":"No, it is a triangle"},{"id":"d","text":"Yes, all house shapes are hexagons"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Count the sides: bottom, right, two roof sides and left. That is 5 sides, so it is a pentagon.', '{"kind":"shape","points":[[1,0],[7,0],[7,4],[4,7],[1,4]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070201', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_easy', 1, 'What is this object called?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"sphere"},{"id":"b","text":"cube"},{"id":"c","text":"cone"},{"id":"d","text":"cylinder"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It is round all over like a ball. It is a sphere.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"sphere"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070202', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_easy', 1, 'A tennis ball is shaped like a sphere.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A tennis ball is round all over, so it is a sphere.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070203', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which thing is shaped like a cylinder?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"a can of soup"},{"id":"b","text":"a dice"},{"id":"c","text":"a tennis ball"},{"id":"d","text":"an ice-cream cone"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A can has a circle at each end and a curved side. That is a cylinder.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070204', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'easy', 1, 'This is a cube. How many faces does it have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'A cube has 6 square faces: top, bottom, front, back, left and right.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"cube"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070205', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'easy', 1, 'Which objects can roll? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"sphere"},{"id":"b","text":"cylinder"},{"id":"c","text":"cube"},{"id":"d","text":"cone"},{"id":"e","text":"rectangular prism"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'Objects with a curved surface can roll: the sphere, the cylinder and the cone. A cube and a prism have only flat faces.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070206', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'easy', 1, 'What is this object called?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"cone"},{"id":"b","text":"square pyramid"},{"id":"c","text":"cylinder"},{"id":"d","text":"triangle"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It has a circle face at the bottom and comes to a point. It is a cone.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"cone"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070207', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'medium', 1, 'Which everyday thing has this shape?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"a cereal box"},{"id":"b","text":"a basketball"},{"id":"c","text":"a party hat"},{"id":"d","text":"a can"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'This is a rectangular prism. A cereal box has rectangle faces just like it.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"rectangular_prism"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070208', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'medium', 1, 'A cube has ___ corners.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"8"'::jsonb, 'A cube has 4 corners on top and 4 on the bottom. 4 + 4 = 8.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070209', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'medium', 1, 'A triangle is a 3D object.', 'true_false', NULL, '"false"'::jsonb, 'A triangle is a flat 2D shape. A 3D object, like a pyramid, can have triangle faces.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070210', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'hard', 1, 'How many faces does this object have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, 'This is a square pyramid. It has 1 square face on the bottom and 4 triangle faces. 1 + 4 = 5.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"square_pyramid"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070211', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'hard', 1, 'Put these objects in order from fewest flat faces to most flat faces.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"sphere"},{"id":"b","text":"cone"},{"id":"c","text":"cylinder"},{"id":"d","text":"cube"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A sphere has no flat faces, a cone has 1, a cylinder has 2 and a cube has 6.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070212', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'hard', 1, 'Which object has 12 edges?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"cube"},{"id":"b","text":"square pyramid"},{"id":"c","text":"cone"},{"id":"d","text":"cylinder"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A cube has 4 edges on top, 4 on the bottom and 4 going up the sides. 4 + 4 + 4 = 12.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070213', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_hard', 1, 'How many corners do 2 cubes have altogether?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"16"'::jsonb, 'Each cube has 8 corners. 8 + 8 = 16.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070214', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_hard', 1, 'How many faces does this object have?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"5"},{"id":"b","text":"6"},{"id":"c","text":"3"},{"id":"d","text":"9"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'This is a triangular prism. It has 2 triangle faces at the ends and 3 rectangle faces around the side. 2 + 3 = 5.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"triangular_prism"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070215', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_hard', 1, 'I have 1 flat face that is a circle. I have 1 curved surface. I come to a point at the top. What am I?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"cone"},{"id":"b","text":"cylinder"},{"id":"c","text":"sphere"},{"id":"d","text":"square pyramid"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A cylinder has 2 circle faces, a sphere has none and a pyramid has a square face. A cone has 1 circle face and a point.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070216', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_easy', 1, 'What is this object called?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"cylinder"},{"id":"b","text":"cone"},{"id":"c","text":"cube"},{"id":"d","text":"sphere"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It has a circle at each end and a curved side. It is a cylinder.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"cylinder"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070217', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_easy', 1, 'Which thing is shaped like a cube?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"a dice"},{"id":"b","text":"a ball"},{"id":"c","text":"a can"},{"id":"d","text":"a party hat"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A dice has 6 square faces, just like a cube.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070218', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_easy', 1, 'A sphere has no corners.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A sphere is curved all over, so it has no corners.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070219', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'easy', 1, 'How many faces does this object have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'This is a rectangular prism, like a box. It has a top, a bottom, a front, a back and 2 ends. That is 6 faces.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"rectangular_prism"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070220', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'easy', 1, 'Which objects have a curved surface? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"cylinder"},{"id":"b","text":"cone"},{"id":"c","text":"sphere"},{"id":"d","text":"cube"},{"id":"e","text":"square pyramid"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'A cylinder, a cone and a sphere all have a curved surface. A cube and a pyramid have only flat faces.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070221', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'easy', 1, 'A cylinder has ___ flat faces.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"2"'::jsonb, 'A cylinder has a flat circle face at each end, so 2 flat faces.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070222', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'medium', 1, 'What is this object called?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"square pyramid"},{"id":"b","text":"cube"},{"id":"c","text":"triangular prism"},{"id":"d","text":"cone"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'It has a square face on the bottom and triangle faces that meet at a point. It is a square pyramid.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"square_pyramid"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070223', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'medium', 1, 'How many edges does a cube have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"12"'::jsonb, 'An edge is where two faces meet. A cube has 4 edges on top, 4 on the bottom and 4 up the sides. That is 12.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070224', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'medium', 1, 'Which object is best for building a tall tower that will not roll away?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"cube"},{"id":"b","text":"sphere"},{"id":"c","text":"cone"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A cube has flat faces, so cubes stack well and do not roll.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070225', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'hard', 1, 'How many corners does this object have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"6"'::jsonb, 'This is a triangular prism. Each triangle end has 3 corners. 3 + 3 = 6.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"triangular_prism"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070226', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'hard', 1, 'A cone and a cylinder both have a flat face that is a circle.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A cone has a circle face on the bottom. A cylinder has a circle face at each end.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070227', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'hard', 1, 'Put these objects in order from fewest corners to most corners.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"sphere"},{"id":"b","text":"cone"},{"id":"c","text":"square pyramid"},{"id":"d","text":"cube"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'A sphere has 0 corners, a cone has 1 point, a square pyramid has 5 corners and a cube has 8.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070228', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_hard', 1, 'How many edges does this object have?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"8"'::jsonb, 'This square pyramid has 4 edges around the square bottom and 4 edges going up to the point. 4 + 4 = 8.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"square_pyramid"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070229', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_hard', 1, 'Which objects have only flat faces? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"cube"},{"id":"b","text":"triangular prism"},{"id":"c","text":"square pyramid"},{"id":"d","text":"cylinder"},{"id":"e","text":"cone"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'A cube, a triangular prism and a square pyramid have only flat faces. A cylinder and a cone have a curved surface too.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070230', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020702', 'very_hard', 1, 'Zoe traces around every face of this cube. What does she draw?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"6 squares"},{"id":"b","text":"6 circles"},{"id":"c","text":"4 triangles"},{"id":"d","text":"1 square"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A cube has 6 faces, and every face is a square. So she draws 6 squares.', '{"kind":"solid","shape":"cube"}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070301', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_easy', 1, 'What is the opposite of left?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"right"},{"id":"b","text":"up"},{"id":"c","text":"down"},{"id":"d","text":"behind"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Left and right are opposite sides.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070302', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_easy', 1, 'The cat is under the table. So the table is above the cat.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'If the cat is under the table, the table must be over it, or above it.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070303', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_easy', 1, 'Look at the map. Which place is in the top row?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the school"},{"id":"b","text":"the shop"},{"id":"c","text":"home"},{"id":"d","text":"the pool"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The school is in the highest row of the map. The others are lower down.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":0,"label":"Home"},{"x":0,"y":3,"label":"Pool"},{"x":2,"y":3,"label":"Park"},{"x":4,"y":1,"label":"Shop"},{"x":4,"y":4,"label":"School"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070304', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'easy', 1, 'Look at the map. Start at home. Go 4 squares right and 1 square up. Where are you?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the shop"},{"id":"b","text":"the park"},{"id":"c","text":"the pool"},{"id":"d","text":"the school"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'From home, count 4 squares to the right, then 1 square up. You land on the shop.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":0,"label":"Home"},{"x":0,"y":3,"label":"Pool"},{"x":2,"y":3,"label":"Park"},{"x":4,"y":1,"label":"Shop"},{"x":4,"y":4,"label":"School"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070305', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'easy', 1, 'Facing the board, the door is on your left. Facing the back of the room, the door is on your ___.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"right"'::jsonb, 'When you turn around to face the other way, left and right swap. So the door is now on your right.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070306', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'easy', 1, 'Ava is in front of Kai. Leo is behind Kai. Put them in order from front to back.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"Ava"},{"id":"b","text":"Kai"},{"id":"c","text":"Leo"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'Ava is in front, Kai is in the middle and Leo is behind Kai.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070307', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'medium', 1, 'Follow the path from home to the park. How many squares long is the path?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["5","5 squares"]'::jsonb, 'The path goes 2 squares right, then 3 squares up. 2 + 3 = 5 squares.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":0,"label":"Home"},{"x":0,"y":3,"label":"Pool"},{"x":2,"y":3,"label":"Park"},{"x":4,"y":1,"label":"Shop"},{"x":4,"y":4,"label":"School"}],"path":[[0,0],[2,0],[2,3]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070308', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'medium', 1, 'Look at the map. Which places are further right than the pool? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"the park"},{"id":"b","text":"the shop"},{"id":"c","text":"the school"},{"id":"d","text":"home"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'The pool is in the first column on the left. The park, shop and school are all further right. Home is in the same column as the pool.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":0,"label":"Home"},{"x":0,"y":3,"label":"Pool"},{"x":2,"y":3,"label":"Park"},{"x":4,"y":1,"label":"Shop"},{"x":4,"y":4,"label":"School"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070309', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'medium', 1, 'Look at the map. The school is straight above the shop.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The shop and the school are in the same column, and the school is higher up. So the school is straight above the shop.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":0,"label":"Home"},{"x":0,"y":3,"label":"Pool"},{"x":2,"y":3,"label":"Park"},{"x":4,"y":1,"label":"Shop"},{"x":4,"y":4,"label":"School"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070310', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'hard', 1, 'Look at the map. Start at the pool. Go 4 squares right and 1 square up. Where are you?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the school"},{"id":"b","text":"the park"},{"id":"c","text":"the shop"},{"id":"d","text":"home"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'From the pool, 4 squares right takes you past the park. Then 1 square up lands on the school.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":0,"label":"Home"},{"x":0,"y":3,"label":"Pool"},{"x":2,"y":3,"label":"Park"},{"x":4,"y":1,"label":"Shop"},{"x":4,"y":4,"label":"School"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070311', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'hard', 1, 'Ben and Zara stand facing each other. Ben puts up his right hand. Which side is it on as Zara looks at him?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"on her left"},{"id":"b","text":"on her right"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'When two people face each other, their sides are swapped. Ben''s right hand is on Zara''s left side.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070312', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'hard', 1, 'Look at the map. To go from the park to the school, go ___ squares right and 1 square up.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"2"'::jsonb, 'The school is 2 columns to the right of the park and 1 row higher. So go 2 squares right and 1 up.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":0,"label":"Home"},{"x":0,"y":3,"label":"Pool"},{"x":2,"y":3,"label":"Park"},{"x":4,"y":1,"label":"Shop"},{"x":4,"y":4,"label":"School"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070313', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_hard', 1, 'Look at the map. Lily starts at home. She goes 4 squares right, then 3 squares up. Which place is 1 square above her?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the school"},{"id":"b","text":"the shop"},{"id":"c","text":"the park"},{"id":"d","text":"the pool"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '4 right from home is under the shop. 3 up passes the shop and stops just below the school. So the school is 1 square above her.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":0,"label":"Home"},{"x":0,"y":3,"label":"Pool"},{"x":2,"y":3,"label":"Park"},{"x":4,"y":1,"label":"Shop"},{"x":4,"y":4,"label":"School"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070314', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_hard', 1, 'Look at the map. Tom walks from the shop to the pool. He goes left, then up. How many squares does he walk?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["6","6 squares"]'::jsonb, 'From the shop, go 4 squares left to reach the pool''s column. Then go 2 squares up to the pool. 4 + 2 = 6.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":0,"label":"Home"},{"x":0,"y":3,"label":"Pool"},{"x":2,"y":3,"label":"Park"},{"x":4,"y":1,"label":"Shop"},{"x":4,"y":4,"label":"School"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070315', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_hard', 1, 'Ella faces the classroom door. The window is on her left. She turns around to face the other way. Where is the window now?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"on her right"},{"id":"b","text":"on her left"},{"id":"c","text":"in front of her"},{"id":"d","text":"behind her"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Turning around swaps left and right. The window was on her left, so now it is on her right.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070316', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_easy', 1, 'Your left hand and your right hand are on opposite sides of your body.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'One hand is on each side of your body, so left and right are opposite sides.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070317', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_easy', 1, 'The cup is on top of the book. Where is the book?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"under the cup"},{"id":"b","text":"on top of the cup"},{"id":"c","text":"beside the cup"},{"id":"d","text":"inside the cup"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'If the cup is on top of the book, the book is under the cup.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070318', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_easy', 1, 'Look at the map of the camping ground. What is straight above the BBQ?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the lake"},{"id":"b","text":"the tent"},{"id":"c","text":"the swings"},{"id":"d","text":"the toilets"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Go straight up from the BBQ in the same column. You reach the lake.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"Tent"},{"x":3,"y":1,"label":"BBQ"},{"x":3,"y":4,"label":"Lake"},{"x":1,"y":3,"label":"Swings"},{"x":5,"y":0,"label":"Toilets"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070319', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'easy', 1, 'Look at the map. How many squares do you go right to get from the tent to the BBQ?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["3","3 squares"]'::jsonb, 'The tent and the BBQ are in the same row. Count the squares to the right: 1, 2, 3.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"Tent"},{"x":3,"y":1,"label":"BBQ"},{"x":3,"y":4,"label":"Lake"},{"x":1,"y":3,"label":"Swings"},{"x":5,"y":0,"label":"Toilets"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070320', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'easy', 1, 'Ned is on the far left. Pip is on the far right. Ola is in the middle. Put them in order from left to right.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"Ned"},{"id":"b","text":"Ola"},{"id":"c","text":"Pip"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c"]'::jsonb, 'Ned is on the left, Ola is in the middle and Pip is on the right.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070321', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'easy', 1, 'The opposite of in front of is ___.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"behind"'::jsonb, 'If something is not in front of you but at your back, it is behind you.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070322', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'medium', 1, 'Look at the map. Follow the path from the tent. Where does it go?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"to the swings"},{"id":"b","text":"to the lake"},{"id":"c","text":"to the BBQ"},{"id":"d","text":"to the toilets"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'The path goes 1 square right from the tent, then 2 squares up. It ends at the swings.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"Tent"},{"x":3,"y":1,"label":"BBQ"},{"x":3,"y":4,"label":"Lake"},{"x":1,"y":3,"label":"Swings"},{"x":5,"y":0,"label":"Toilets"}],"path":[[0,1],[1,1],[1,3]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070323', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'medium', 1, 'Look at the map. Start at the BBQ. Go 2 squares right and 1 square down. Where are you?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the toilets"},{"id":"b","text":"the lake"},{"id":"c","text":"the tent"},{"id":"d","text":"the swings"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'From the BBQ, count 2 squares right, then 1 square down. You reach the toilets.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"Tent"},{"x":3,"y":1,"label":"BBQ"},{"x":3,"y":4,"label":"Lake"},{"x":1,"y":3,"label":"Swings"},{"x":5,"y":0,"label":"Toilets"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070324', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'medium', 1, 'Look at the map. Which places are higher up than the BBQ? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"the lake"},{"id":"b","text":"the swings"},{"id":"c","text":"the tent"},{"id":"d","text":"the toilets"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b"]'::jsonb, 'The lake and the swings are in higher rows. The tent is in the same row as the BBQ and the toilets are lower.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"Tent"},{"x":3,"y":1,"label":"BBQ"},{"x":3,"y":4,"label":"Lake"},{"x":1,"y":3,"label":"Swings"},{"x":5,"y":0,"label":"Toilets"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070325', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'hard', 1, 'Look at the map. The toilets are further right than the BBQ.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'The toilets are in the last column on the right. The BBQ is further left, so the toilets are further right.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"Tent"},{"x":3,"y":1,"label":"BBQ"},{"x":3,"y":4,"label":"Lake"},{"x":1,"y":3,"label":"Swings"},{"x":5,"y":0,"label":"Toilets"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070326', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'hard', 1, 'Max walks to school and the park is on his right. He walks home along the same road. Where is the park now?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"on his left"},{"id":"b","text":"on his right"},{"id":"c","text":"in front of him"},{"id":"d","text":"behind him"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Walking back the other way turns him around, so left and right swap. The park is on his left.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070327', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'hard', 1, 'Look at the map. To go from the tent to the lake, go 3 squares right and ___ squares up.', 'fill_blank', NULL, '"3"'::jsonb, 'The lake is 3 columns right of the tent and 3 rows higher. So go 3 right and 3 up.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"Tent"},{"x":3,"y":1,"label":"BBQ"},{"x":3,"y":4,"label":"Lake"},{"x":1,"y":3,"label":"Swings"},{"x":5,"y":0,"label":"Toilets"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070328', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_hard', 1, 'Look at the map. Jo walks from the swings to the toilets. She goes right, then down. How many squares does she walk?', 'short_answer', NULL, '["7","7 squares"]'::jsonb, 'From the swings, go 4 squares right to reach the toilets'' column. Then go 3 squares down. 4 + 3 = 7.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"Tent"},{"x":3,"y":1,"label":"BBQ"},{"x":3,"y":4,"label":"Lake"},{"x":1,"y":3,"label":"Swings"},{"x":5,"y":0,"label":"Toilets"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070329', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_hard', 1, 'Look at the map. Sam starts at the lake. He goes 2 squares left and 1 square down. Then he goes 1 square left and 2 squares down. Where is he?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"the tent"},{"id":"b","text":"the swings"},{"id":"c","text":"the BBQ"},{"id":"d","text":"the toilets"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '2 left and 1 down from the lake takes Sam to the swings. Then 1 left and 2 down takes him to the tent.', '{"kind":"grid","columns":6,"rows":5,"map":true,"points":[{"x":0,"y":1,"label":"Tent"},{"x":3,"y":1,"label":"BBQ"},{"x":3,"y":4,"label":"Lake"},{"x":1,"y":3,"label":"Swings"},{"x":5,"y":0,"label":"Toilets"}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002070330', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020703', 'very_hard', 1, 'Lucy faces the board. The bin is on her right. She turns around to face the back wall. Then she turns around again. Where is the bin now?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"on her right"},{"id":"b","text":"on her left"},{"id":"c","text":"behind her"},{"id":"d","text":"in front of her"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Turning around once puts the bin on her left. Turning around again puts her back where she started, so the bin is on her right.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080101', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'very_easy', 1, 'Ms Lee wants to find out the class''s favourite fruit. What should she do?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Ask each child"},{"id":"b","text":"Guess"},{"id":"c","text":"Ask only one child"},{"id":"d","text":"Count the windows"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'To find out what the class likes, she needs to ask everyone and record their answers.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080102', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'very_easy', 1, 'Look at the table. How many children have a cat?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"4"'::jsonb, 'Find the Cat row and read across. It says 4.', '{"kind":"table","headings":["Pet","Children"],"rows":[["Dog",6],["Cat",4],["Fish",2]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080103', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'very_easy', 1, 'Tally marks are a quick way to keep count as you collect data.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'You make one mark for each answer, then count the marks at the end.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080104', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'easy', 1, 'Kim counted cars: 3 red, 5 blue, 2 white and 4 black. Put the colours in order from most to fewest.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"blue"},{"id":"b","text":"black"},{"id":"c","text":"red"},{"id":"d","text":"white"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, '5 blue, then 4 black, then 3 red, then 2 white.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080105', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'easy', 1, 'Look at the picture graph. How many children chose netball?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"3"'::jsonb, 'Count the stars in the Netball row. There are 3, and each star is 1 child.', '{"kind":"picture_graph","title":"Favourite sport","thing":"children","each":1,"rows":[{"label":"Cricket","count":5},{"label":"Netball","count":3},{"label":"Soccer","count":4}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080106', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'easy', 1, 'Sam asked children, ''Do you like rain?'' 7 said yes and 5 said no. How many children did Sam ask?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"12"'::jsonb, 'Every child said yes or no. 7 + 5 = 12 children.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080107', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'medium', 1, 'Which question is best for making a picture graph of favourite colours?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Which is your favourite: red, blue, green or yellow?"},{"id":"b","text":"Do you like colours?"},{"id":"c","text":"How old are you?"},{"id":"d","text":"What is your name?"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Giving a few colours to choose from sorts the answers into groups, which makes a clear picture graph.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080108', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'medium', 1, 'Look at the table. Which are true? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"8 kangaroos were seen"},{"id":"b","text":"More emus than wombats were seen"},{"id":"c","text":"5 wombats were seen"},{"id":"d","text":"12 animals were seen altogether"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","d"]'::jsonb, 'The table shows 8 kangaroos, 3 emus and 1 wombat. 3 is more than 1. 8 + 3 + 1 = 12. Only 1 wombat was seen, not 5.', '{"kind":"table","headings":["Animal","Number seen"],"rows":[["Kangaroo",8],["Emu",3],["Wombat",1]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080109', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'medium', 1, 'In a picture graph, all the pictures should be the same size and lined up.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'If the pictures are the same size and lined up, you can compare the rows fairly.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080110', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'hard', 1, 'Here are the favourite drinks of some children: milk, juice, water, milk, juice, milk. How many chose milk?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"3"'::jsonb, 'Count each ''milk'' in the list: 1, 2, 3.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080111', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'hard', 1, 'Tim wants to find out how children get to school. Which answers should go in his table?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"walk, car, bus, bike"},{"id":"b","text":"red, blue, green"},{"id":"c","text":"Monday, Tuesday, Friday"},{"id":"d","text":"cat, dog, fish"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'His question is about getting to school, so the groups are ways to travel: walk, car, bus and bike.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080112', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'hard', 1, 'Look at the picture graph. How many children were asked altogether?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"12"'::jsonb, 'Add up all the rows: 6 + 2 + 4 = 12 children.', '{"kind":"picture_graph","title":"Fruit eaten at recess","thing":"children","each":1,"rows":[{"label":"Apple","count":6},{"label":"Banana","count":2},{"label":"Orange","count":4}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080113', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'very_hard', 1, 'Bella saw 4 magpies in the morning and 5 more magpies in the afternoon. She saw 6 galahs. How many more magpies than galahs did she see?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"3"'::jsonb, 'Magpies: 4 + 5 = 9. Galahs: 6. 9 − 6 = 3 more magpies.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080114', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'very_hard', 1, 'Put the steps for making a picture graph in order.', 'ordering', '[{"id":"a","text":"Ask a question"},{"id":"b","text":"Collect the answers"},{"id":"c","text":"Count each group"},{"id":"d","text":"Draw the pictures in rows"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b","c","d"]'::jsonb, 'First decide your question, then collect answers, then count each group, and last draw the graph.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080115', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'very_hard', 1, '24 children voted for a class pet. Fish got 10 votes and dog got 9 votes. The rest chose rabbit. How many chose rabbit?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"5"},{"id":"b","text":"19"},{"id":"c","text":"4"},{"id":"d","text":"6"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, '10 + 9 = 19 chose fish or dog. 24 − 19 = 5 chose rabbit.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080116', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'very_easy', 1, 'Mr Brown asks each child, ''What is your favourite ice cream?'' What is he doing?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Collecting data"},{"id":"b","text":"Drawing a map"},{"id":"c","text":"Telling the time"},{"id":"d","text":"Measuring"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'Asking a question and writing down the answers is collecting data.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080117', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'very_easy', 1, 'Look at the table. How many votes did blue get?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"7"'::jsonb, 'Find the Blue row and read across. It says 7.', '{"kind":"table","headings":["Colour","Votes"],"rows":[["Red",5],["Blue",7],["Green",3]]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080118', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'very_easy', 1, 'Before you make a picture graph, you need to collect some data.', 'true_false', NULL, '"true"'::jsonb, 'A picture graph shows data, so you must collect the data first.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080119', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'easy', 1, 'Lunch orders: pie, sushi, pie, wrap, pie, sushi. How many children ordered sushi?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"2"'::jsonb, 'Count each ''sushi'' in the list: 1, 2.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080120', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'easy', 1, 'What is the best way to keep count while children vote?', 'multiple_choice', '[{"id":"a","text":"Make a tally"},{"id":"b","text":"Try to remember"},{"id":"c","text":"Write nothing down"},{"id":"d","text":"Guess at the end"}]'::jsonb, '"a"'::jsonb, 'A tally gives one mark for each vote, so you don''t lose count.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080121', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'easy', 1, 'Look at the picture graph. How many children come by car?', 'short_answer', NULL, '"5"'::jsonb, 'Count the stars in the Car row. There are 5.', '{"kind":"picture_graph","title":"How we get to school","thing":"children","each":1,"rows":[{"label":"Walk","count":3},{"label":"Car","count":5},{"label":"Bus","count":2}]}'::jsonb, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
  ('61000000-0000-0000-0000-000002080122', '51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000020801', 'medium', 1, 'Which questions could you ask to collect data about pets? Choose all that are right.', 'multi_select', '[{"id":"a","text":"What pet do you have?"},{"id":"b","text":"How many pets do you have?"},{"id":"c","text":"What is 2 + 2?"},{"id":"d","text":"What time is it?"}]'::jsonb, '["a","b"]'::jsonb, 'Only the first two questions are about pets. The others are not.', NULL, NULL, '90000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001'),
